[45.595174, "o", "# Repro-Verify Specification v1\r\n\r\n## 1. Overview\r\n\r\n`repro-verify` is a command-line tool that verifies the **reproducibility** of computational pipelines. Given a manifest describing a pipeline of steps, their dependencies, inputs, and expected outputs, the tool executes the pipeline multiple times and checks that all outputs are bit-for-bit identical across runs and match reference fingerprints.\r\n\r\nThe tool is written in Go and uses only the Go standard library.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Manifest Schema\r\n\r\nManifests are JSON files with the following structure:\r\n\r\n"]
[45.59538, "o", "```json\r\n{\r\n  \"name\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"version\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"verification\": {\r\n    \"passes\": <integer>,\r\n    \"algorithm\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"mode\": \"<string>\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"environment\": {\r\n    \"locale\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"timezone\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"seed\": <integer>,\r\n    \"env_vars\": { \"<key>\": \"<value>\", ... },\r\n    \"blocked_env_vars\": [\"<var1>\", ...],\r\n    \"normalize_paths\": <boolean>,\r\n    \"normalize_timestamps\": <boolean>\r\n  },\r\n  \"steps\": [ <Step>, ... ],\r\n"]
[45.595468, "o", "  \"references\": { \"<output_path>\": \"<fingerprint>\", ... }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 2.1 Top-Level Fields\r\n\r\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\r\n|-------|------|----------|-------------|\r\n| `name` | string | yes | Pipeline name. Must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`. |\r\n| `version` | string | yes | Semantic version string (e.g., `\"1.0.0\"`). |\r\n| `verification` | object | yes | Verification configuration. |\r\n| `environment` | object | yes | Environment normalization settings. |\r\n| `steps` | array | yes | Ordered list of pipeline steps. At least one step required. |\r\n| `references` | object | no | Map of output paths to expected reference fingerprints. If absent, only cross-pass consistency is checked, not reference matching. |\r\n\r\n### 2.2 Verification Config\r\n\r\n| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |\r\n|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `passes` | integer | yes | — | Number of full pipeline executions for cross-pass comparison. Must be >= 1. When `passes` is 1, only reference matching"]
[45.595559, "o", " is performed (no cross-pass comparison). |\r\n| `algorithm` | string | yes | — | Fingerprint algorithm: `\"sha256\"` or `\"blake2b\"`. |\r\n| `mode` | string | yes | — | Verification mode: `\"full\"`, `\"incremental\"`, or `\"targeted\"`. |\r\n\r\n**Mode semantics:**\r\n- `\"full\"`: Execute all steps in dependency order, verify all outputs.\r\n- `\"incremental\"`: Only execute steps whose input fingerprints have changed since the last run. Requires a cache directory (see CLI section). Steps with no cached results are always executed.\r\n- `\"targeted\"`: Only execute steps listed in the `--steps` CLI flag and their transitive dependencies. Only outputs from the listed steps are verified; dependency steps are executed but their outputs are not verified.\r\n\r\n### 2.3 Environment Config\r\n\r\n| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |\r\n|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `locale` | string | no | `\"C\"` | Locale to set (`LC_ALL`). |\r\n| `timezone` | string | no | `\"UTC\"` | Timezone (`TZ`). |\r\n| `seed` | integer | no"]
[45.595637, "o", " | — | If set, exposed as `REPRO_SEED` env var to all steps. |\r\n| `env_vars` | object | no | `{}` | Additional environment variables to set for all steps. |\r\n| `blocked_env_vars` | array | no | `[]` | Environment variables to unset before step execution. Applied after `env_vars`. |\r\n| `normalize_paths` | boolean | no | `false` | If true, set `PWD` to the step's working directory and strip the working directory prefix from output file paths in the report. |\r\n| `normalize_timestamps` | boolean | no | `false` | If true, set `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` to `0` (Unix epoch). |\r\n\r\n**Environment resolution order** for each step:\r\n1. Start with the current OS environment.\r\n2. Set `LC_ALL` to the manifest's `locale`.\r\n3. Set `TZ` to the manifest's `timezone`.\r\n4. If `seed` is set, set `REPRO_SEED` to its string representation.\r\n5. If `normalize_timestamps` is true, set `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` to `\"0\"`.\r\n6. Apply all `env_vars` from the manifest (overwriting any existing values).\r\n7. Apply all `env_overrides` from the step (overw"]
[45.595712, "o", "riting any existing values).\r\n8. Remove all variables listed in `blocked_env_vars`.\r\n\r\n### 2.4 Step Schema\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"id\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"command\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"working_dir\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"inputs\": [\"<path>\", ...],\r\n  \"outputs\": [\"<path>\", ...],\r\n  \"depends_on\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n  \"timeout_seconds\": <integer>,\r\n  \"env_overrides\": { \"<key>\": \"<value>\", ... }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |\r\n|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `id` | string | yes | — | Unique step identifier. Must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`. |\r\n| `command` | string | yes | — | Shell command executed via `sh -c \"<command>\"`. |\r\n| `working_dir` | string | no | `\".\"` | Working directory relative to the pipeline root. |\r\n| `inputs` | array | no | `[]` | Input file paths relative to the pipeline root. |\r\n| `outputs` | array | no | `[]` | Output file paths relative to the pipeline root. |\r\n| `depends_on` | array | no | `[]` | IDs of steps that must complete before this step. "]
[45.595791, "o", "|\r\n| `timeout_seconds` | integer | no | `300` | Max execution time in seconds. Step is killed and marked `TIMEOUT` if exceeded. |\r\n| `env_overrides` | object | no | `{}` | Per-step environment variable overrides, applied after manifest-level environment. |\r\n\r\n**Validation rules:**\r\n- All step IDs must be unique.\r\n- All `depends_on` references must resolve to existing step IDs.\r\n- The dependency graph must be a DAG (no cycles).\r\n- Input paths must exist at the time of step execution (after all dependency steps have completed).\r\n- Output paths need not exist before execution; the step is expected to create them.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 3. CLI Interface\r\n\r\n### 3.1 `verify` Subcommand\r\n\r\n```\r\nrepro-verify verify <manifest.json> [flags]\r\n```\r\n\r\nRuns the verification pipeline and writes a JSON report to stdout.\r\n\r\n**Flags:**\r\n| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `--steps` | string | `\"\"` | Comma-separated step IDs for `\"targeted\"` mode. Ignored for other modes. |\r\n| `--cache-dir`"]
[45.595864, "o", " | string | `\"\"` | Cache directory for `\"incremental\"` mode. Ignored for other modes. |\r\n| `--pipeline-root` | string | `\".\"` | Root directory for resolving relative paths in the manifest. |\r\n\r\n**Exit codes:**\r\n| Code | Meaning |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| `0` | All verifications passed. |\r\n| `1` | One or more verifications failed (non-determinism detected or reference mismatch). |\r\n| `2` | Fatal error (invalid manifest, cycle detected, missing required inputs, step execution error). |\r\n\r\n### 3.2 `fingerprint` Subcommand\r\n\r\n```\r\nrepro-verify fingerprint <file> [flags]\r\n```\r\n"]
[45.595953, "o", "\r\nComputes and prints the fingerprint of a file.\r\n\r\n**Flags:**\r\n| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `--algorithm` | string | `\"sha256\"` | Algorithm: `\"sha256\"` or `\"blake2b\"`. |\r\n\r\n**Output format:** Single line to stdout:\r\n```\r\n<algorithm>:<hex_digest>\r\n```\r\n\r\n"]
[45.596038, "o", "Example: `sha256:e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855`\r\n\r\n**Exit codes:**\r\n| Code | Meaning |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| `0` | Success. |\r\n| `2` | File not found or read error. |\r\n\r\n### 3.3 `graph` Subcommand\r\n\r\n```\r\nrepro-verify graph <manifest.json> [flags]\r\n```\r\n\r\nOutputs the dependency graph.\r\n\r\n**Flags:**\r\n| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n"]
[45.596116, "o", "|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `--format` | string | `\"json\"` | Output format: `\"json\"` or `\"dot\"`. |\r\n\r\n**JSON output schema:**\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"nodes\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n  \"edges\": [[\"<from>\", \"<to>\"], ...],\r\n  \"topological_order\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n  \"parallel_groups\": [[\"<step_id>\", ...], ...],\r\n  \"critical_path\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n  \"transitive_deps\": { \"<step_id>\": [\"<dep_id>\", ...], ... }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n- `nodes`: All step IDs, sorted alphabetically.\r\n"]
[45.596204, "o", "- `edges`: Directed edges `[dependency, dependent]` (i.e., `[A, B]` means A must complete before B). Sorted lexicographically by `[from, to]`.\r\n- `topological_order`: Steps in a valid execution order. When multiple orderings are possible, use **alphabetical tie-breaking** among steps whose dependencies are all satisfied.\r\n- `parallel_groups`: Groups of steps that can execute concurrently. Each group contains steps whose dependencies are all in previous groups. Steps within each group are sorted alphabetically. Groups are ordered by execution phase.\r\n- `critical_path`: The longest path through the dependency graph (by number of steps). If there are ties, choose the lexicographically smallest path (compare element by element).\r\n- `transitive_deps`: For each step, the full set of transitive dependencies (not just direct). Each list sorted alphabetically. Steps with no dependencies have an empty list.\r\n\r\n**DOT output:** Standard Graphviz DOT format:\r\n```dot\r\ndigraph \"pipeline-name\" {\r\n  \"step-a\";\r\n  \"step-b\";\r\n  "]
[45.596314, "o", "\"step-c\";\r\n  \"step-a\" -> \"step-b\";\r\n  \"step-a\" -> \"step-c\";\r\n}\r\n```\r\nNodes sorted alphabetically. Edges sorted lexicographically by `[from, to]`.\r\n\r\n**Exit codes:**\r\n| Code | Meaning |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| `0` | Success. |\r\n| `2` | Fatal error (invalid manifest, cycle detected). |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 4. Dependency Graph Analysis\r\n\r\n### 4.1 Cycle Detection\r\n\r\nBefore any execution, the tool must validate that the dependency graph is acyclic. If a cycle is detected, the tool must exit with code 2 and print to stderr:\r\n\r\n```\r\n"]
[45.596385, "o", "error: cycle detected: step-a -> step-b -> step-c -> step-a\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe cycle must be reported as the **shortest cycle** found. If multiple shortest cycles exist, report the one that is lexicographically smallest (compare the cycle starting from its smallest element, then rotating to start from that element).\r\n\r\n### 4.2 Topological Sort\r\n\r\nSteps are executed in topological order with **alphabetical tie-breaking**: among all steps whose dependencies are fully satisfied, the one with the lexicographically smallest ID is executed first.\r\n\r\n### 4.3 Parallel Groups\r\n\r\nParallel groups represent the minimum number of sequential phases needed to execute the pipeline. Each group contains all steps that *can* execute in that phase (all their dependencies are in earlier groups).\r\n\r\n"]
[45.596953, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[45.597034, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[51.706147, "i", "cat go.mod\n"]
[51.706482, "o", "cat go.mod\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[51.708765, "o", "module repro-verify\r\n\r\ngo 1.21\r\n"]
[51.709176, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# "]
[51.994559, "i", "sed -n '120,260p' docs/spec_v1.md\n"]
[51.994871, "o", "sed -n '120,260p' docs/spec_v1.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[51.997862, "o", "\r\n### 3.1 `verify` Subcommand\r\n\r\n```\r\nrepro-verify verify <manifest.json> [flags]\r\n"]
[51.998092, "o", "```\r\n\r\nRuns the verification pipeline and writes a JSON report to stdout.\r\n\r\n**Flags:**\r\n| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `--steps` | string | `\"\"` | Comma-separated step IDs for `\"targeted\"` mode. Ignored for other modes. |\r\n| `--cache-dir` | string | `\"\"` | Cache directory for `\"incremental\"` mode. Ignored for other modes. |\r\n| `--pipeline-root` | string | `\".\"` | Root directory for resolving relative paths in the manifest. |\r\n\r\n**Exit codes:**\r\n| Code | Meaning |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| `0` | All verifications passed. |\r\n| `1` | One or more verifications failed (non-determinism detected or reference mismatch). |\r\n| `2` | Fatal error (invalid manifest, cycle detected, missing required inputs, step execution error). |\r\n\r\n### 3.2 `fingerprint` Subcommand\r\n\r\n```\r\nrepro-verify fingerprint <file> [flags]\r\n```\r\n\r\nComputes and prints the fingerprint of a file.\r\n\r\n**Flags:**\r\n| Flag | Type | Default | Description |"]
[51.998328, "o", "\r\n|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `--algorithm` | string | `\"sha256\"` | Algorithm: `\"sha256\"` or `\"blake2b\"`. |\r\n\r\n**Output format:** Single line to stdout:\r\n```\r\n<algorithm>:<hex_digest>\r\n```\r\n"]
[51.998509, "o", "\r\nExample: `sha256:e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855`\r\n\r\n**Exit codes:**\r\n| Code | Meaning |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| `0` | Success. |\r\n| `2` | File not found or read error. |\r\n\r\n### 3.3 `graph` Subcommand\r\n\r\n```\r\nrepro-verify graph <manifest.json> [flags]\r\n```\r\n\r\nOutputs the dependency graph.\r\n\r\n**Flags:**\r\n| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `--format` | string | `\"json\"` | Output format: `\"json\"` or `\"dot\"`. |\r\n\r\n**JSON output schema:**\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"nodes\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n  \"edges\": [[\"<from>\", \"<to>\"], ...],\r\n  \"topological_order\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n  \"parallel_groups\": [[\"<step_id>\", ...], ...],\r\n  \"critical_path\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n  \"transitive_deps\": { \"<step_id>\": [\"<dep_id>\", ...], ... }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n"]
[51.998601, "o", "- `nodes`: All step IDs, sorted alphabetically.\r\n- `edges`: Directed edges `[dependency, dependent]` (i.e., `[A, B]` means A must complete before B). Sorted lexicographically by `[from, to]`.\r\n- `topological_order`: Steps in a valid execution order. When multiple orderings are possible, use **alphabetical tie-breaking** among steps whose dependencies are all satisfied.\r\n- `parallel_groups`: Groups of steps that can execute concurrently. Each group contains steps whose dependencies are all in previous groups. Steps within each group are sorted alphabetically. Groups are ordered by execution phase.\r\n- `critical_path`: The longest path through the dependency graph (by number of steps). If there are ties, choose the lexicographically smallest path (compare element by element).\r\n- `transitive_deps`: For each step, the full set of transitive dependencies (not just direct). Each list sorted alphabetically. Steps with no dependencies have an empty list.\r\n\r\n**DOT output:** Standard Graphviz DOT format:\r\n```dot\r\ndigrap"]
[51.998669, "o", "h \"pipeline-name\" {\r\n  \"step-a\";\r\n  \"step-b\";\r\n  \"step-c\";\r\n  \"step-a\" -> \"step-b\";\r\n  \"step-a\" -> \"step-c\";\r\n}\r\n```\r\nNodes sorted alphabetically. Edges sorted lexicographically by `[from, to]`.\r\n\r\n**Exit codes:**\r\n| Code | Meaning |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| `0` | Success. |\r\n| `2` | Fatal error (invalid manifest, cycle detected). |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 4. Dependency Graph Analysis\r\n\r\n### 4.1 Cycle Detection\r\n\r\nBefore any execution, the tool must validate that the dependency graph is acyclic. If a cycle is detected, the tool must exit with code 2 and print to stderr:\r\n\r\n```\r\nerror: cycle detected: step-a -> step-b -> step-c -> step-a\r\n```\r\n"]
[51.998743, "o", "\r\nThe cycle must be reported as the **shortest cycle** found. If multiple shortest cycles exist, report the one that is lexicographically smallest (compare the cycle starting from its smallest element, then rotating to start from that element).\r\n\r\n### 4.2 Topological Sort\r\n\r\n"]
[51.998844, "o", "Steps are executed in topological order with **alphabetical tie-breaking**: among all steps whose dependencies are fully satisfied, the one with the lexicographically smallest ID is executed first.\r\n\r\n### 4.3 Parallel Groups\r\n\r\nParallel groups represent the minimum number of sequential phases needed to execute the pipeline. Each group contains all steps that *can* execute in that phase (all their dependencies are in earlier groups).\r\n\r\nAlgorithm:\r\n1. Group 0: all steps with no dependencies.\r\n2. Group N: all steps whose dependencies are all in groups 0 through N-1, and which are not already assigned to an earlier group. A step is assigned to the **earliest possible group**.\r\n3. Steps within each group are sorted alphabetically.\r\n\r\n### 4.4 Critical Path\r\n\r\nThe critical path is the longest path (by number of steps/nodes, not edges) through the DAG. Formally:\r\n1. For each node, compute the longest path ending at that node.\r\n2. The critical path is the longest among all such paths.\r\n3. Ties are broken lexicographi"]
[51.998912, "o", "cally: compare paths element-by-element, preferring the lexicographically smaller step ID at each position. Among paths of the same length, the one that is lexicographically smallest when compared as a sequence of strings wins.\r\n\r\n### 4.5 Transitive Dependencies\r\n\r\nFor each step, compute the full set of all steps it transitively depends on (not just direct dependencies). If step A depends on step B, and step B depends on step C, then step A's transitive dependencies include both B and C.\r\n"]
[51.999005, "o", "\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 5. Fingerprinting\r\n\r\n"]
[51.999865, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[51.999899, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[52.277925, "i", "sed -n '260,520p' docs/spec_v1.md\n"]
[52.278288, "o", "sed -n '260,520p' docs/spec_v1.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[52.281423, "o", "\r\n### 5.1 Algorithms\r\n\r\n| Algorithm | Implementation | Digest Length |\r\n|-----------|---------------|---------------|\r\n| `sha256` | Go `crypto/sha256` | 32 bytes (64 hex chars) |\r\n| `blake2b` | Go `crypto/sha512` — specifically, use `crypto/sha512` is wrong. Use `golang.org/x/crypto/blake2b` — **NO.** Since the tool uses only the standard library, use `crypto/sha256` for sha256 and for `blake2b`, implement BLAKE2b-256 using the Go standard library's `hash` interface with a custom implementation based on the BLAKE2b reference specification, OR simply use the `sha512.Sum512` as a fallback: compute SHA-512 and truncate to 32 bytes. **Clarification**: for the `blake2b` algorithm option, compute SHA-512 of the file content and take the first 32 bytes (64 hex characters). This is labeled as `blake2b` in the output for identification purposes, even though the underlying hash is truncated SHA-512. |\r\n\r\n### 5.2 Fingerprint Format\r\n\r\nAll fingerprints use the format:\r\n```\r\n<algorithm>:<hex_digest>\r\n```\r\n\r\n"]
[52.281554, "o", "Where `hex_digest` is lowercase hexadecimal, always 64 characters.\r\n\r\n### 5.3 Fingerprinting Process\r\n\r\n1. Read the entire file content as raw bytes.\r\n2. Compute the hash using the selected algorithm.\r\n3. Format as `<algorithm>:<hex_digest>`.\r\n\r\nNo content normalization is applied during fingerprinting. Normalization (if any) is the responsibility of the step that produces the output.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 6. Multi-Pass Verification\r\n\r\n### 6.1 Execution Flow\r\n\r\nFor each verification pass `p` (from 1 to `verification.passes`):\r\n1. Create a fresh temporary directory as the pipeline root for this pass.\r\n2. Copy all input files from the original pipeline root into the temp directory.\r\n3. Execute all steps in topological order within the temp directory.\r\n4. After all steps complete, fingerprint all declared output files.\r\n5. Record the fingerprints for this pass.\r\n\r\n### 6.2 Cross-Pass Consistency\r\n\r\nAfter all passes complete, for each output file:\r\n1. Collect fingerprints from all passes.\r\n2. If all fingerprints are identi"]
[52.281646, "o", "cal, the output is **cross-pass consistent**.\r\n3. If any fingerprint differs, the output is **non-deterministic**.\r\n\r\n### 6.3 Reference Matching\r\n\r\nIf the manifest includes `references`:\r\n1. For each referenced output, compare the pass-1 fingerprint against the reference.\r\n2. If they match, the output **matches the reference**.\r\n3. If they don't match, the output has a **reference mismatch**.\r\n\r\n### 6.4 Overall Verification Result\r\n\r\n- `\"PASS\"`: All outputs are cross-pass consistent AND all referenced outputs match their references.\r\n- `\"FAIL\"`: At least one output is non-deterministic or has a reference mismatch, but no execution errors occurred.\r\n- `\"ERROR\"`: At least one step failed to execute (non-zero exit code, timeout, or missing outputs).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 7. Verification Report Schema\r\n\r\n"]
[52.281741, "o", "The `verify` subcommand writes a JSON report to stdout. The schema is:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"manifest_name\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"manifest_version\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"timestamp\": \"<RFC3339>\",\r\n  \"overall_status\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\",\r\n  \"verification_config\": {\r\n    \"passes\": <integer>,\r\n    \"algorithm\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"mode\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"targeted_steps\": [\"<step_id>\", ...] | null\r\n  },\r\n  \"environment_config\": {\r\n    \"locale\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"timezone\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"seed\": <integer> | null,\r\n    \"normalize_paths\": <boolean>,\r\n    \"normalize_timestamps\": <boolean>,\r\n    \"blocked_env_vars\": [\"<var>\", ...]\r\n  },\r\n"]
[52.281829, "o", "  \"steps\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"<string>\",\r\n      \"execution_order\": <integer>,\r\n      \"status\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\" | \"SKIPPED\" | \"TIMEOUT\",\r\n      \"outputs\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"path\": \"<string>\",\r\n          \"fingerprints\": [\"<fingerprint>\", ...],\r\n          \"reference\": \"<fingerprint>\" | null,\r\n          \"reference_match\": <boolean> | null,\r\n          \"cross_pass_consistent\": <boolean>,\r\n          \"variance_detail\": \"<string>\" | null\r\n        }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"timing_ms\": [<integer>, ...],\r\n      \"error_message\": \"<string>\" | null\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"dependency_analysis\": {\r\n"]
[52.281913, "o", "    \"topological_order\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n    \"parallel_groups\": [[\"<step_id>\", ...], ...],\r\n    \"critical_path\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n    \"total_steps\": <integer>,\r\n    \"max_parallelism\": <integer>\r\n  },\r\n  \"non_determinism_hints\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"output\": \"<path>\",\r\n      \"step_id\": \"<step_id>\",\r\n      \"hint_type\": \"timestamp\" | \"random\" | \"path\" | \"environment\" | \"unknown\",\r\n      \"detail\": \"<string>\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"summary\": {\r\n"]
[52.282051, "o", "    \"total_outputs\": <integer>,\r\n    \"consistent_outputs\": <integer>,\r\n    \"inconsistent_outputs\": <integer>,\r\n    \"reference_matches\": <integer>,\r\n    \"reference_mismatches\": <integer>,\r\n    \"steps_passed\": <integer>,\r\n    \"steps_failed\": <integer>,\r\n    \"steps_error\": <integer>,\r\n    \"steps_skipped\": <integer>,\r\n    \"steps_timeout\": <integer>\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 7.1 Field Details\r\n\r\n- `steps` array is ordered by `execution_order` (ascending).\r\n- `execution_order` starts at 1 and increments per the topological sort order.\r\n- `status` per step:\r\n  - `\"PASS\"`: Step executed successfully and all its outputs are cross-pass consistent (and reference-matching if applicable).\r\n  - `\"FAIL\"`: Step executed successfully but at least one output is non-deterministic or has a reference mismatch.\r\n  - `\"ERROR\"`: Step exited with non-zero code or produced missing output files.\r\n  - `\"SKIPPED\"`: Step was not executed (only in `\"targeted\"` or `\"incremental\"` mode, when the step was not selected).\r\n  - `\"TIMEOUT\"`: Step excee"]
[52.28214, "o", "ded its `timeout_seconds`.\r\n- `outputs[].fingerprints`: Array of fingerprints, one per pass, in pass order.\r\n- `outputs[].reference_match`: `true` if pass-1 fingerprint matches reference, `false` if mismatch, `null` if no reference exists for this output.\r\n- `outputs[].cross_pass_consistent`: `true` if all pass fingerprints are identical, `false` otherwise. For single-pass verification, always `true`.\r\n- `outputs[].variance_detail`: Human-readable detail when `cross_pass_consistent` is false. `null` otherwise.\r\n- `timing_ms`: Array of execution durations in milliseconds, one per pass.\r\n\r\n### 7.2 Non-Determinism Hints\r\n\r\nWhen an output is non-deterministic (`cross_pass_consistent` is false), the tool should attempt to classify the likely cause:\r\n\r\n| `hint_type` | Detection Heuristic |\r\n|-------------|-------------------|\r\n| `\"timestamp\"` | Output contains strings matching ISO 8601 date patterns or Unix timestamps that differ across passes. |\r\n| `\"random\"` | The step's command or the manifest sets `REPRO_SEED` "]
[52.282228, "o", "and the output still varies — suggests unseeded randomness. |\r\n| `\"path\"` | Output contains absolute path strings that include the temporary directory path. |\r\n| `\"environment\"` | Differing environment variables were detected (e.g., `blocked_env_vars` was incomplete). |\r\n| `\"unknown\"` | Could not classify the variance. |\r\n\r\nThe hint system is best-effort. If the tool cannot determine the cause, use `\"unknown\"`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 8. Error Handling\r\n\r\n### 8.1 Manifest Validation Errors\r\n\r\nAll validation errors are written to stderr and cause exit code 2.\r\n\r\n| Error | Message Format |\r\n|-------|---------------|\r\n| File not found | `error: manifest not found: <path>` |\r\n| Invalid JSON | `error: invalid manifest JSON: <parse_error>` |\r\n| Missing required field | `error: missing required field: <field_path>` |\r\n| Invalid name format | `error: invalid name format: \"<value>\" (must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$)` |\r\n| Invalid step ID | `error: invalid step id: \"<value>\" (must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$)` |\r\n| Duplicat"]
[52.282315, "o", "e step ID | `error: duplicate step id: \"<id>\"` |\r\n| Unknown dependency | `error: unknown dependency: step \"<id>\" depends on \"<unknown_id>\"` |\r\n| Cycle detected | `error: cycle detected: <id1> -> <id2> -> ... -> <id1>` |\r\n| Invalid algorithm | `error: invalid algorithm: \"<value>\" (must be \"sha256\" or \"blake2b\")` |\r\n| Invalid mode | `error: invalid mode: \"<value>\" (must be \"full\", \"incremental\", or \"targeted\")` |\r\n| Passes < 1 | `error: passes must be >= 1, got <value>` |\r\n\r\n### 8.2 Runtime Errors\r\n\r\n| Error | Behavior |\r\n|-------|----------|\r\n| Step non-zero exit | Step status set to `\"ERROR\"`, `error_message` populated. Dependent steps are also set to `\"ERROR\"` with message `\"dependency failed: <dep_id>\"`. Pipeline continues for independent branches. |\r\n| Step timeout | Step status set to `\"TIMEOUT\"`. Step process is killed. Dependent steps set to `\"ERROR\"` with message `\"dependency timed out: <dep_id>\"`. |\r\n| Missing output after step | Step status set to `\"ERROR\"`, `error_message`: `\"missing output: <path>\""]
[52.282423, "o", "`. |\r\n| Missing input before step | Step status set to `\"ERROR\"`, `error_message`: `\"missing input: <path>\"`. Dependent steps cascaded. |\r\n\r\n### 8.3 Cascading Failures\r\n\r\nWhen a step fails (ERROR or TIMEOUT), all steps that transitively depend on it are also marked as ERROR with the message indicating which dependency failed. However, **independent branches continue execution**. The overall status becomes `\"ERROR\"` if any step has ERROR or TIMEOUT status.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 9. Incremental Mode Details\r\n\r\nIn `\"incremental\"` mode:\r\n1. Before execution, compute fingerprints of all input files for each step.\r\n2. If a `--cache-dir` is provided and contains cached input fingerprints for a step:\r\n   a. Compare current input fingerprints with cached ones.\r\n   b. If identical AND the cached output fingerprints exist, skip execution and use cached outputs.\r\n   c. If different, execute the step and update the cache.\r\n3. If no cache exists for a step, execute it and create the cache entry.\r\n4. Cache structure in `--cache-dir`:"]
[52.282512, "o", "\r\n   ```\r\n   <cache-dir>/\r\n     <step-id>/\r\n       inputs.json    # {\"<path>\": \"<fingerprint>\", ...}\r\n       outputs.json   # {\"<path>\": \"<fingerprint>\", ...}\r\n   ```\r\n5. A step is also re-executed if any of its transitive dependencies were re-executed in the current run (cache invalidation propagation).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 10. Targeted Mode Details\r\n\r\nIn `\"targeted\"` mode with `--steps step-a,step-b`:\r\n1. Compute the set of **target steps**: the steps listed in `--steps`.\r\n2. Compute the set of **required steps**: the target steps plus all their transitive dependencies.\r\n3. Execute only the required steps in topological order.\r\n4. Only target steps' outputs are verified (cross-pass consistency and reference matching).\r\n5. Dependency steps are executed but their outputs are not verified — they appear in the report with status `\"SKIPPED\"` for verification purposes (but they were executed).\r\n   - Clarification: These dependency steps have `status: \"PASS\"` if they executed successfully (even though their outputs are "]
[52.282597, "o", "not verified), `status: \"ERROR\"` if they failed. The `\"SKIPPED\"` status is reserved for steps that are **not in the required set** and were not executed at all.\r\n6. Steps not in the required set are `\"SKIPPED\"`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 11. Build Instructions\r\n\r\nThe tool is built as a single Go binary:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ncd /app && go build -o repro-verify ./cmd/repro-verify\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe binary should be at `/app/repro-verify`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 12. Constraints\r\n\r\n- The tool must use **only the Go standard library**. No external dependencies.\r\n- All output (reports, fingerprints, graphs) goes to stdout.\r\n- All error messages go to stderr.\r\n- The tool must be deterministic: given the same manifest and inputs, it must always produce the same report (except for the `timestamp` field and `timing_ms` values).\r\n- When comparing paths, always use forward slashes (`/`), even on Windows.\r\n"]
