[59.786495, "o", "   320\t## 7. Verification Report Schema\r\n   321\t\r\n   322\tThe `verify` subcommand writes a JSON report to stdout. The schema is:\r\n   323\t\r\n   324\t```json\r\n   325\t{\r\n   326\t  \"manifest_name\": \"<string>\",\r\n   327\t  \"manifest_version\": \"<string>\",\r\n   328\t  \"timestamp\": \"<RFC3339>\",\r\n   329\t  \"overall_status\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\",\r\n   330\t  \"verification_config\": {\r\n   331\t    \"passes\": <integer>,\r\n   332\t    \"algorithm\": \"<string>\",\r\n   333\t    \"mode\": \"<string>\",\r\n"]
[59.786647, "o", "   334\t    \"targeted_steps\": [\"<step_id>\", ...] | null\r\n   335\t  },\r\n   336\t  \"environment_config\": {\r\n   337\t    \"locale\": \"<string>\",\r\n   338\t    \"timezone\": \"<string>\",\r\n   339\t    \"seed\": <integer> | null,\r\n   340\t    \"normalize_paths\": <boolean>,\r\n   341\t    \"normalize_timestamps\": <boolean>,\r\n   342\t    \"blocked_env_vars\": [\"<var>\", ...]\r\n   343\t  },\r\n   344\t  \"steps\": [\r\n   345\t    {\r\n   346\t      \"id\": \"<string>\",\r\n   347\t      \"execution_order\": <integer>,\r\n   348\t      \"status\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\" | \"SKIPPED\" | \"TIMEOUT\",\r\n   349\t      \"outputs\": [\r\n   350\t        {\r\n   351\t          \"path\": \"<string>\",\r\n   352\t          \"fingerprints\": [\"<fingerprint>\", ...],\r\n   353\t          \"reference\": \"<fingerprint>\" | null,\r\n   354\t          \"reference_match\": <boolean> | null,\r\n   355\t          \"cross_pass_consistent\": <boolean>,\r\n"]
[59.786726, "o", "   356\t          \"variance_detail\": \"<string>\" | null\r\n   357\t        }\r\n   358\t      ],\r\n   359\t      \"timing_ms\": [<integer>, ...],\r\n   360\t      \"error_message\": \"<string>\" | null\r\n   361\t    }\r\n   362\t  ],\r\n   363\t  \"dependency_analysis\": {\r\n   364\t    \"topological_order\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n   365\t    \"parallel_groups\": [[\"<step_id>\", ...], ...],\r\n"]
[59.786804, "o", "   366\t    \"critical_path\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n   367\t    \"total_steps\": <integer>,\r\n   368\t    \"max_parallelism\": <integer>\r\n   369\t  },\r\n   370\t  \"non_determinism_hints\": [\r\n   371\t    {\r\n   372\t      \"output\": \"<path>\",\r\n   373\t      \"step_id\": \"<step_id>\",\r\n   374\t      \"hint_type\": \"timestamp\" | \"random\" | \"path\" | \"environment\" | \"unknown\",\r\n   375\t      \"detail\": \"<string>\"\r\n   376\t    }\r\n   377"]
[59.78687, "o", "\t  ],\r\n   378\t  \"summary\": {\r\n   379\t    \"total_outputs\": <integer>,\r\n   380\t    \"consistent_outputs\": <integer>,\r\n   381\t    \"inconsistent_outputs\": <integer>,\r\n   382\t    \"reference_matches\": <integer>,\r\n   383\t    \"reference_mismatches\": <integer>,\r\n   384\t    \"steps_passed\": <integer>,\r\n   385\t    \"steps_failed\": <integer>,\r\n"]
[59.786983, "o", "   386\t    \"steps_error\": <integer>,\r\n   387\t    \"steps_skipped\": <integer>,\r\n   388\t    \"steps_timeout\": <integer>\r\n   389\t  }\r\n   390\t}\r\n   391\t```\r\n   392\t\r\n"]
[59.787062, "o", "   393\t### 7.1 Field Details\r\n   394\t\r\n   395\t- `steps` array is ordered by `execution_order` (ascending).\r\n   396\t- `execution_order` starts at 1 and increments per the topological sort order.\r\n   397\t- `status` per step:\r\n   398\t  - `\"PASS\"`: Step executed successfully and all its outputs are cross-pass consistent (and reference-matching if applicable).\r\n   399\t  - `\"FAIL\"`: Step executed successfully but at least one output is non-deterministic or has a reference mismatch.\r\n   400\t  - `\"ERROR\"`: Step exited with non-zero code or produced missing output files.\r\n   401\t  - `\"SKIPPED\"`: Step was not executed (only in `\"targeted\"` or `\"incremental\"` mode, when the step was not selected).\r\n   402\t  - `\"TIMEOUT\"`: Step exceeded its `timeout_seconds`.\r\n   403\t- `outputs[].fingerprints`: Array of fingerprints, one per pass, in pass order.\r\n   404\t- `outputs[].reference_match`: `true` if pass-1 fingerprint matches reference, `false` if mismatch, `null` if no reference exists for this output.\r\n   405\t- `outputs[].cr"]
[59.787151, "o", "oss_pass_consistent`: `true` if all pass fingerprints are identical, `false` otherwise. For single-pass verification, always `true`.\r\n   406\t- `outputs[].variance_detail`: Human-readable detail when `cross_pass_consistent` is false. `null` otherwise.\r\n   407\t- `timing_ms`: Array of execution durations in milliseconds, one per pass.\r\n   408\t\r\n   409\t### 7.2 Non-Determinism Hints\r\n   410\t\r\n   411\tWhen an output is non-deterministic (`cross_pass_consistent` is false), the tool should attempt to classify the likely cause:\r\n   412\t\r\n   413\t| `hint_type` | Detection Heuristic |\r\n   414\t|-------------|-------------------|\r\n   415\t| `\"timestamp\"` | Output contains strings matching ISO 8601 date patterns or Unix timestamps that differ across passes. |\r\n   416\t| `\"random\"` | The step's command or the manifest sets `REPRO_SEED` and the output still varies — suggests unseeded randomness. |\r\n   417\t| `\"path\"` | Output contains absolute path strings that include the temporary directory path. |\r\n   418\t"]
[59.78722, "o", "| `\"environment\"` | Differing environment variables were detected (e.g., `blocked_env_vars` was incomplete). |\r\n   419\t| `\"unknown\"` | Could not classify the variance. |\r\n   420\t\r\n   421\tThe hint system is best-effort. If the tool cannot determine the cause, use `\"unknown\"`.\r\n   422\t\r\n   423\t---\r\n   424\t\r\n   425\t## 8. Error Handling\r\n   426\t\r\n   427\t### 8.1 Manifest Validation Errors\r\n   428\t\r\n   429\tAll validation errors are written to stderr and cause exit code 2.\r\n   430\t\r\n   431\t| Error | Message Format |\r\n   432\t|-------|---------------|\r\n   433\t| File not found | `error: manifest not found: <path>` |\r\n   434\t| Invalid JSON | `error: invalid manifest JSON: <parse_error>` |\r\n   435\t| Missing required field | `error: missing required field: <field_path>` |\r\n"]
[59.787296, "o", "   436\t| Invalid name format | `error: invalid name format: \"<value>\" (must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$)` |\r\n   437\t| Invalid step ID | `error: invalid step id: \"<value>\" (must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$)` |\r\n   438\t| Duplicate step ID | `error: duplicate step id: \"<id>\"` |\r\n   439\t| Unknown dependency | `error: unknown dependency: step \"<id>\" depends on \"<unknown_id>\"` |\r\n   440\t| Cycle detected | `error: cycle detected: <id1> -> <id2> -> ... -> <id1>` |\r\n   441\t| Invalid algorithm | `error: invalid algorithm: \"<value>\" (must be \"sha256\" or \"blake2b\")` |\r\n   442\t| Invalid mode | `error: invalid mode: \"<value>\" (must be \"full\", \"incremental\", or \"targeted\")` |\r\n   443\t| Passes < 1 | `error: passes must be >= 1, got <value>` |\r\n   444\t\r\n   445\t### 8.2 Runtime Errors\r\n"]
[59.787365, "o", "   446\t\r\n   447\t| Error | Behavior |\r\n   448\t|-------|----------|\r\n   449\t| Step non-zero exit | Step status set to `\"ERROR\"`, `error_message` populated. Dependent steps are also set to `\"ERROR\"` with message `\"dependency failed: <dep_id>\"`. Pipeline continues for independent branches. |\r\n   450\t| Step timeout | Step status set to `\"TIMEOUT\"`. Step process is killed. Dependent steps set to `\"ERROR\"` with message `\"dependency timed out: <dep_id>\"`. |\r\n   451\t| Missing output after step | Step status set to `\"ERROR\"`, `error_message`: `\"missing output: <path>\"`. |\r\n   452\t| Missing input before step | Step status set to `\"ERROR\"`, `error_message`: `\"missing input: <path>\"`. Dependent steps cascaded. |\r\n   453\t\r\n"]
[59.787436, "o", "   454\t### 8.3 Cascading Failures\r\n   455\t\r\n   456\tWhen a step fails (ERROR or TIMEOUT), all steps that transitively depend on it are also marked as ERROR with the message indicating which dependency failed. However, **independent branches continue execution**. The overall status becomes `\"ERROR\"` if any step has ERROR or TIMEOUT status.\r\n   457\t\r\n   458\t---\r\n   459\t\r\n   460\t## 9. Incremental Mode Details\r\n"]
