[69.753577, "o", "   460\t## 9. Incremental Mode Details\r\n   461\t\r\n   462\tIn `\"incremental\"` mode:\r\n   463\t1. Before execution, compute fingerprints of all input files for each step.\r\n   464\t2. If a `--cache-dir` is provided and contains cached input fingerprints for a step:\r\n   465\t   a. Compare current input fingerprints with cached ones.\r\n   466\t   b. If identical AND the cached output fingerprints exist, skip execution and use cached outputs.\r\n"]
[69.753723, "o", "   467\t   c. If different, execute the step and update the cache.\r\n   468\t3. If no cache exists for a step, execute it and create the cache entry.\r\n   469\t4. Cache structure in `--cache-dir`:\r\n   470\t   ```\r\n   471\t   <cache-dir>/\r\n   472\t     <step-id>/\r\n   473\t       inputs.json    # {\"<path>\": \"<fingerprint>\", ...}\r\n   474\t       outputs.json   # {\"<path>\": \"<fingerprint>\", ...}\r\n   475\t   ```\r\n   476\t5. A step is also re-executed if any of its transitive dependencies were re-executed in the current run (cache invalidation propagation).\r\n   477\t\r\n   478\t---\r\n   479\t\r\n   480\t## 10. Targeted Mode Details\r\n   481\t\r\n   482\tIn `\"targeted\"` mode with `--steps step-a,step-b`:\r\n   483\t1. Compute the set of **target steps**: the steps listed in `--steps`.\r\n   484\t2. Compute the set of **required steps**: the target steps plus all their transitive dependencies.\r\n   485\t3. Execute only the required steps in topological order.\r\n   486\t4. Only target steps' outputs are verified (cross-pass consistency and reference mat"]
[69.753813, "o", "ching).\r\n   487\t5. Dependency steps are executed but their outputs are not verified — they appear in the report with status `\"SKIPPED\"` for verification purposes (but they were executed).\r\n   488\t   - Clarification: These dependency steps have `status: \"PASS\"` if they executed successfully (even though their outputs are not verified), `status: \"ERROR\"` if they failed. The `\"SKIPPED\"` status is reserved for steps that are **not in the required set** and were not executed at all.\r\n   489\t6. Steps not in the required set are `\"SKIPPED\"`.\r\n   490\t\r\n   491\t---\r\n   492\t\r\n   493\t## 11. Build Instructions\r\n   494\t\r\n   495\tThe tool is built as a single Go binary:\r\n   496\t\r\n   497\t```bash\r\n   498\tcd /app && go build -o repro-verify ./cmd/repro-verify\r\n   499\t```\r\n   500\t\r\n   501\tThe binary should be at `/app/repro-verify`.\r\n"]
[69.753878, "o", "   502\t\r\n   503\t---\r\n   504\t\r\n   505\t## 12. Constraints\r\n   506\t\r\n   507\t- The tool must use **only the Go standard library**. No external dependencies.\r\n   508\t- All output (reports, fingerprints, graphs) goes to stdout.\r\n   509\t- All error messages go to stderr.\r\n   510\t- The tool must be deterministic: given the same manifest and inputs, it must always produce the same report (except for the `timestamp` field and `timing_ms` values).\r\n   511\t"]
[69.754035, "o", "- When comparing paths, always use forward slashes (`/`), even on Windows.\r\n"]
[69.754426, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
