[2656.891363, "o", "1:# Repro-Verify Specification v2\r\n12:## 13. Verification Policy Engine\r\n14:### 13.1 Policy Section in Manifest\r\n40:### 13.2 Rule Schema\r\n58:### 13.3 Rule Types\r\n60:#### `allow_variance`\r\n75:#### `min_consistency_rate`\r\n94:#### `required_steps`\r\n109:#### `ignore_steps`\r\n122:### 13.4 Policy Evaluation Flow\r\n140:### 13.5 Report Additions\r\n175:### 13.6 Exit Code with Policy\r\n184:### 13.7 Policy Validation Errors\r\n199:## 14. `diff` Subcommand\r\n201:### 14.1 Usage\r\n214:### 14.2 JSON Output Schema\r\n"]
[2656.891529, "o", "271:### 14.3 Comparison Logic\r\n302:### 14.4 Text Output Format\r\n324:### 14.5 Exit Codes\r\n332:### 14.6 Input Validation\r\n"]
[2656.891953, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[2656.892019, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2657.160288, "i", "sed -n '1,220p' /app/docs/spec_v2.md\n"]
[2657.160613, "o", "sed -n '1,220p' /app/docs/spec_v2.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2657.163646, "o", "# Repro-Verify Specification v2\r\n\r\nThis document extends `spec_v1.md` with two major features added in v2:\r\n\r\n1. **Verification Policy Engine** — rule-based pass/fail criteria\r\n2. **`diff` Subcommand** — compare two verification reports\r\n\r\nAll v1 behavior remains unchanged unless explicitly overridden below.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 13. Verification Policy Engine\r\n\r\n### 13.1 Policy Section in Manifest\r\n\r\n"]
[2657.163797, "o", "The manifest gains an optional `policy` section:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"policy\": {\r\n    \"default_action\": \"strict\",\r\n    \"rules\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"<string>\",\r\n        \"type\": \"<string>\",\r\n        \"params\": { ... },\r\n        \"action\": \"allow\"\r\n      }\r\n    ]\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |\r\n|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `policy` | object | no | — | If absent, strict verification applies (identical to v1 behavior). |\r\n| `policy.default_action` | string | no | `\"strict\"` | `\"strict\"`: all outputs must match. `\"lenient\"`: treat non-determinism as warnings unless a rule specifically requires a match. |\r\n| `policy.rules` | array | yes (if policy present) | — | Ordered list of policy rules. Rules are evaluated in order; the **first matching rule** for a given step/output determines the action. |\r\n\r\n### 13.2 Rule Schema\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"id\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"type\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"params\": { ... },\r\n  \"action\": \"<string>\"\r\n"]
[2657.163879, "o", "}\r\n```\r\n\r\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\r\n|-------|------|----------|-------------|\r\n| `id` | string | yes | Unique rule identifier. Must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`. |\r\n| `type` | string | yes | Rule type (see below). |\r\n| `params` | object | yes | Type-specific parameters. |\r\n| `action` | string | yes | `\"allow\"`, `\"warn\"`, or `\"require\"`. |\r\n"]
[2657.163989, "o", "\r\n### 13.3 Rule Types\r\n\r\n#### `allow_variance`\r\n\r\nAllows specific outputs to be non-deterministic without failing verification.\r\n\r\n**Params:**\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"output_pattern\": \"<glob pattern>\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n`output_pattern` is a glob pattern matched against output file paths (e.g., `\"*.log\"`, `\"tmp/*\"`). Uses `filepath.Match` semantics.\r\n\r\n**Behavior:** For outputs matching the pattern: if the output is non-deterministic (different across passes) or has a reference mismatch, and the rule's action is `\"allow\"`, the step's effective status changes from `FAIL` to `PASS` (for that output). If action is `\"warn\"`, the status stays `FAIL` but a warning is emitted. If action is `\"require\"`, the output **must** be non-deterministic (if it's actually consistent, the rule marks it as a policy violation).\r\n\r\n#### `min_consistency_rate`\r\n\r\nRequires that at least a specified fraction of passes produce identical output, but does not require 100% consistency.\r\n\r\n**Params:**\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"rate\": <float>,\r\n  \"step_pattern\": \"<g"]
[2657.164059, "o", "lob pattern>\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n- `rate`: A float between 0.0 and 1.0. For example, `0.75` means at least 75% of passes must agree.\r\n- `step_pattern`: Glob pattern matching step IDs. Use `\"*\"` for all steps.\r\n\r\n**Behavior:** For each output of matching steps, compute the **majority rate**: the fraction of passes that produced the most common fingerprint. If `majority_rate >= rate` and action is `\"allow\"`, treat the output as effectively consistent. If `majority_rate < rate` and action is `\"require\"`, it's a policy violation.\r\n\r\n**Majority rate computation:** Given N passes and fingerprints f1..fN, count occurrences of each unique fingerprint. The majority rate is `max_count / N`. For single-pass verification, majority rate is always 1.0.\r\n\r\n#### `required_steps`\r\n"]
[2657.164126, "o", "\r\nSpecifies that only certain steps are required to pass; failures in other steps don't affect the overall policy status.\r\n\r\n**Params:**\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"steps\": [\"<step_id>\", ...]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Behavior:** When evaluating policy_overall_status:\r\n- If action is `\"require\"`: all listed steps must have status PASS (after other policy rules). If any listed step is FAIL/ERROR/TIMEOUT, overall policy status is FAIL/ERROR.\r\n- If action is `\"allow\"`: unlisted steps that are FAIL/ERROR are forgiven — they don't affect policy_overall_status. Listed steps still follow normal rules.\r\n\r\n#### `ignore_steps`\r\n\r\nCompletely ignores certain steps in policy evaluation.\r\n\r\n**Params:**\r\n"]
[2657.164244, "o", "```json\r\n{\r\n  \"steps\": [\"<step_id>\", ...]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Behavior:** Steps in the list are excluded from policy_overall_status computation entirely, regardless of their actual status.\r\n\r\n### 13.4 Policy Evaluation Flow\r\n\r\n1. **Normal verification** runs first (exactly as v1), producing raw step statuses and output results.\r\n2. **Rule evaluation** in order:\r\n   - For each rule, identify which steps/outputs it matches.\r\n   - Apply the rule's effect based on its action:\r\n     - `\"allow\"`: If matched and the condition is satisfied, change the effective status of affected outputs/steps from FAIL→PASS.\r\n     - `\"warn\"`: If matched and the condition is satisfied, keep status but add a warning.\r\n     - `\"require\"`: If matched and the condition is NOT satisfied, mark as policy violation (FAIL).\r\n   - First matching rule wins for each output — subsequent rules don't override.\r\n3. **Recompute `policy_overall_status`:**\r\n   - After applying all rules, compute effective step statuses:\r\n     - A step is effectively PASS "]
[2657.164336, "o", "if all its outputs are effectively PASS (or it had no outputs / was SKIPPED).\r\n     - A step is effectively FAIL if any output is effectively FAIL.\r\n     - ERROR and TIMEOUT statuses are never changed by policy (they indicate execution failures, not verification results).\r\n   - Under `\"strict\"` default: all steps (except those matched by `ignore_steps`) must be effectively PASS for policy_overall_status=PASS.\r\n   - Under `\"lenient\"` default: all steps with no matching rule that are FAIL become WARN (not FAIL), so policy_overall_status is PASS unless a `\"require\"` rule is violated.\r\n\r\n### 13.5 Report Additions\r\n\r\nThe verification report gains a `policy_evaluation` section (only present when `policy` is defined in manifest):\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"policy_evaluation\": {\r\n    \"policy_overall_status\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\",\r\n    \"default_action\": \"strict\" | \"lenient\",\r\n    \"rules_evaluated\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"rule_id\": \"<string>\",\r\n        \"rule_type\": \"<string>\",\r\n        \"matched_steps\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n"]
[2657.164402, "o", "        \"matched_outputs\": [\"<path>\", ...],\r\n        \"action\": \"allow\" | \"warn\" | \"require\",\r\n        \"effect\": \"applied\" | \"not_applicable\" | \"violation\",\r\n        \"details\": \"<string>\"\r\n      }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"effective_step_statuses\": {\r\n      \"<step_id>\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\" | \"SKIPPED\" | \"TIMEOUT\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"warnings\": [\"<string>\", ...]\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n- `rules_evaluated`: One entry per rule showing what it matched and its effect.\r\n"]
[2657.164469, "o", "  - `\"applied\"`: The rule matched and changed something (allowed a variance, etc.)\r\n  - `\"not_applicable\"`: The rule didn't match anything or its condition wasn't relevant.\r\n  - `\"violation\"`: A `\"require\"` rule's condition was not met.\r\n- `effective_step_statuses`: Map of step ID to effective status after policy rules. Only includes steps whose effective status differs from raw status, or steps explicitly matched by a rule.\r\n- `warnings`: Human-readable warning messages from `\"warn\"` action rules.\r\n\r\n### 13.6 Exit Code with Policy\r\n\r\nWhen a policy is present, the exit code follows `policy_overall_status`:\r\n- 0: `policy_overall_status` is PASS\r\n- 1: `policy_overall_status` is FAIL\r\n- 2: `policy_overall_status` is ERROR, or manifest validation error\r\n\r\n"]
[2657.164534, "o", "The raw `overall_status` in the report body is **unchanged** from v1 behavior — it still reflects the strict verification result. The policy only affects exit code and the separate `policy_evaluation` section.\r\n\r\n### 13.7 Policy Validation Errors\r\n\r\n| Error | Message |\r\n|-------|---------|\r\n| Duplicate rule ID | `error: duplicate policy rule id: \"<id>\"` |\r\n| Unknown rule type | `error: unknown policy rule type: \"<type>\"` |\r\n| Invalid action | `error: invalid policy action: \"<action>\" (must be \"allow\", \"warn\", or \"require\")` |\r\n| Invalid default_action | `error: invalid default_action: \"<value>\" (must be \"strict\" or \"lenient\")` |\r\n| Invalid rate | `error: invalid min_consistency_rate: rate must be between 0.0 and 1.0` |\r\n| Unknown step in required_steps | `error: unknown step in policy rule \"<rule_id>\": \"<step_id>\"` |\r\n"]
[2657.164601, "o", "| Unknown step in ignore_steps | `error: unknown step in policy rule \"<rule_id>\": \"<step_id>\"` |\r\n| Missing required params | `error: policy rule \"<rule_id>\" missing required param: \"<param>\"` |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 14. `diff` Subcommand\r\n\r\n### 14.1 Usage\r\n\r\n"]
[2657.16463, "o", "```\r\nrepro-verify diff <baseline.json> <current.json> [flags]\r\n```\r\n\r\nCompares two verification reports and outputs a structured change analysis.\r\n\r\n**Flags:**\r\n| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `--format` | string | `\"json\"` | Output format: `\"json\"` or `\"text\"`. |\r\n\r\n### 14.2 JSON Output Schema\r\n"]
[2657.164654, "o", "\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n"]
[2657.164676, "o", "  \"baseline\": {\r\n    \"manifest_name\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"manifest_version\": \"<string>\",\r\n"]
[2657.165237, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[2657.165273, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2657.489354, "i", "sed -n '220,520p' /app/docs/spec_v2.md\n"]
[2657.489694, "o", "sed -n '220,520p' /app/docs/spec_v2.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2657.492705, "o", "    \"manifest_version\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"overall_status\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"timestamp\": \"<string>\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"current\": {\r\n    \"manifest_name\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"manifest_version\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"overall_status\": \"<string>\",\r\n"]
[2657.49287, "o", "    \"timestamp\": \"<string>\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"comparison_timestamp\": \"<RFC3339>\",\r\n  \"status_transition\": {\r\n    \"from\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\",\r\n    \"to\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\",\r\n    \"type\": \"regression\" | \"improvement\" | \"unchanged\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"step_changes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"step_id\": \"<string>\",\r\n      \"change_type\": \"added\" | \"removed\" | \"modified\" | \"unchanged\",\r\n      \"baseline_status\": \"<string>\" | null,\r\n      \"current_status\": \"<string>\" | null,\r\n      \"status_transition\": \"regression\" | \"improvement\" | \"unchanged\" | null,\r\n      \"output_changes\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"path\": \"<string>\",\r\n          \"change_type\": \"added\" | \"removed\" | \"fingerprint_changed\" | \"consistency_changed\" | \"reference_changed\" | \"unchanged\",\r\n          \"details\": {\r\n            \"baseline_fingerprints\": [\"<fp>\", ...] | null,\r\n            \"current_fingerprints\": [\"<fp>\", ...] | null,\r\n            \"baseline_consistent\": <boolean> | null,\r\n            \"current_consistent\": <boolean> | null,\r\n            \"baseline_reference_match"]
[2657.493106, "o", "\": <boolean> | null,\r\n            \"current_reference_match\": <boolean> | null\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      ]\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"summary\": {\r\n    \"steps_added\": <integer>,\r\n    \"steps_removed\": <integer>,\r\n    \"steps_modified\": <integer>,\r\n    \"steps_unchanged\": <integer>,\r\n    \"regressions\": <integer>,\r\n    \"improvements\": <integer>,\r\n    \"total_output_changes\": <integer>\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 14.3 Comparison Logic\r\n\r\n**Step matching:** Steps are matched by `step_id` between baseline and current.\r\n- A step in current but not in baseline is `\"added\"`.\r\n- A step in baseline but not in current is `\"removed\"`.\r\n- A step in both is `\"modified\"` if any of its attributes changed, `\"unchanged\"` otherwise.\r\n\r\n**Output matching:** Within matched steps, outputs are matched by `path`.\r\n- Output change types:\r\n  - `\"added\"`: Output in current but not baseline.\r\n  - `\"removed\"`: Output in baseline but not current.\r\n  - `\"fingerprint_changed\"`: The pass-1 fingerprint differs.\r\n"]
[2657.493192, "o", "  - `\"consistency_changed\"`: The `cross_pass_consistent` value changed.\r\n  - `\"reference_changed\"`: The `reference_match` value changed.\r\n  - `\"unchanged\"`: No changes.\r\n  - An output can only have one `change_type`. Priority: `added` > `removed` > `fingerprint_changed` > `consistency_changed` > `reference_changed` > `unchanged`.\r\n\r\n**Status ordering for transition detection:**\r\n\r\n```\r\nPASS(4) > FAIL(3) > ERROR(2) > TIMEOUT(1) > SKIPPED(0)\r\n```\r\n\r\n- **Regression**: current status has lower rank than baseline status.\r\n- **Improvement**: current status has higher rank than baseline status.\r\n- **Unchanged**: same rank.\r\n\r\nThe `step_changes` array is sorted by `step_id` alphabetically.\r\n\r\n**The `regressions` count** in summary is the number of steps where `status_transition` is `\"regression\"`. **The `improvements` count** is the number with `\"improvement\"`.\r\n\r\n### 14.4 Text Output Format\r\n\r\n"]
[2657.493276, "o", "```\r\nVerification Report Diff\r\n========================\r\nBaseline: <name>@<version> (<status>) at <timestamp>\r\nCurrent:  <name>@<version> (<status>) at <timestamp>\r\nOverall:  <from> → <to> [<type>]\r\n\r\nStep Changes:\r\n  + <step_id> [<status>]                           # added\r\n  - <step_id> [<status>]                           # removed\r\n  ~ <step_id> [<old_status> → <new_status>]        # modified with status change\r\n"]
[2657.493345, "o", "  = <step_id>                                       # unchanged\r\n    Output: <path> — <change_type>                  # per output if modified\r\n\r\nSummary: <added> added, <removed> removed, <modified> modified, <unchanged> unchanged\r\n         <regressions> regressions, <improvements> improvements\r\n```\r\n\r\n"]
[2657.493462, "o", "Steps are listed in alphabetical order. Only modified steps show their output changes.\r\n\r\n### 14.5 Exit Codes\r\n\r\n| Code | Meaning |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| `0` | No regressions detected. |\r\n| `1` | At least one regression detected. |\r\n| `2` | Error (file not found, invalid JSON, not a valid verification report). |\r\n\r\n### 14.6 Input Validation\r\n\r\nBoth input files must be valid verification reports (containing at minimum `manifest_name`, `overall_status`, and `steps` array). If either file is missing, not valid JSON, or not a valid report, exit with code 2 and print to stderr:\r\n- `error: diff baseline not found: <path>`\r\n"]
[2657.493528, "o", "- `error: diff current not found: <path>`\r\n- `error: invalid report: <path>: <reason>`\r\n"]
[2657.494015, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[2657.494115, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2657.774044, "i", "sed -n '1,220p' cmd/repro-verify/main.go\n"]
[2657.774403, "o", "sed -n '1,220p' cmd/repro-verify/main.go\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2657.777372, "o", "package main\r\n\r\nimport (\r\n\t\"fmt\"\r\n\t\"os\"\r\n)\r\n\r\n"]
[2657.777489, "o", "func main() {\r\n\tif len(os.Args) < 2 {\r\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"usage: repro-verify <verify|fingerprint|graph> ...\")\r\n\t\tos.Exit(2)\r\n\t}\r\n\tswitch os.Args[1] {\r\n\tcase \"verify\":\r\n\t\tverifyCmd(os.Args[2:])\r\n\tcase \"fingerprint\":\r\n\t\tfingerprintCmd(os.Args[2:])\r\n\tcase \"graph\":\r\n\t\tgraphCmd(os.Args[2:])\r\n\tdefault:\r\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"error: unknown subcommand %q\\n\", os.Args[1])\r\n\t\tos.Exit(2)\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n"]
[2657.777996, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[2657.778082, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2658.070604, "i", "sed -n '1,260p' cmd/repro-verify/manifest.go\n"]
[2658.070985, "o", "sed -n '1,260p' cmd/repro-verify/manifest.go"]
[2658.071083, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2658.073901, "o", "package main\r\n\r\nimport (\r\n\t\"encoding/json\"\r\n\t\"fmt\"\r\n\t\"os\"\r\n\t\"regexp\"\r\n\t\"strings\"\r\n"]
[2658.074056, "o", ")\r\n\r\nvar nameRe = regexp.MustCompile(`^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`)\r\n\r\ntype Manifest struct {\r\n\tName    string            `json:\"name\"`\r\n\tVersion string            `json:\"version\"`\r\n\tVerify  VerifyConfig      `json:\"verification\"`\r\n\tEnv     EnvironmentConfig `json:\"environment\"`\r\n\tSteps   []Step            `json:\"steps\"`\r\n\tRefs    map[string]string `json:\"references\"`\r\n}\r\n\r\ntype VerifyConfig struct {\r\n\tPasses    int    `json:\"passes\"`\r\n\tAlgorithm string `json:\"algorithm\"`\r\n\tMode      string `json:\"mode\"`\r\n}\r\n\r\ntype EnvironmentConfig struct {\r\n\tLocale              string            `json:\"locale\"`\r\n\tTimezone            string            `json:\"timezone\"`\r\n\tSeed                *int              `json:\"seed\"`\r\n\tEnvVars             map[string]string `json:\"env_vars\"`\r\n"]
[2658.074193, "o", "\tBlockedEnvVars      []string          `json:\"blocked_env_vars\"`\r\n\tNormalizePaths      bool              `json:\"normalize_paths\"`\r\n\tNormalizeTimestamps bool              `json:\"normalize_timestamps\"`\r\n}\r\n\r\ntype Step struct {\r\n\tID           string            `json:\"id\"`\r\n\tCommand      string            `json:\"command\"`\r\n\tWorkingDir   string            `json:\"working_dir\"`\r\n\tInputs       []string          `json:\"inputs\"`\r\n\tOutputs      []string          `json:\"outputs\"`\r\n\tDependsOn    []string          `json:\"depends_on\"`\r\n\tTimeoutSecs  int               `json:\"timeout_seconds\"`\r\n\tEnvOverrides map[string]string `json:\"env_overrides\"`\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunc loadManifest(path string) (*Manifest, error) {\r\n\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(path)\r\n\tif err != nil {\r\n\t\tif os.IsNotExist(err) {\r\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"manifest not found: %s\", path)\r\n\t\t}\r\n"]
[2658.074271, "o", "\t\treturn nil, err\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\traw := map[string]json.RawMessage{}\r\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &raw); err != nil {\r\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid manifest JSON: %s\", err.Error())\r\n\t}\r\n\tfor _, field := range []string{\"name\", \"version\", \"verification\", \"environment\", \"steps\"} {\r\n\t\tif _, ok := raw[field]; !ok {\r\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"missing required field: %s\", field)\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tvar m Manifest\r\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(data, &m); err != nil {\r\n"]
[2658.074341, "o", "\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid manifest JSON: %s\", err.Error())\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tif m.Name == \"\" {\r\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"missing required field: name\")\r\n\t}\r\n\tif !nameRe.MatchString(m.Name) {\r\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid name format: %q (must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$)\", m.Name)\r\n\t}\r\n\tif m.Version == \"\" {\r\n\t\t"]
[2658.074408, "o", "return nil, fmt.Errorf(\"missing required field: version\")\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tvraw := map[string]json.RawMessage{}\r\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw[\"verification\"], &vraw); err != nil {\r\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid manifest JSON: %s\", err.Error())\r\n\t}\r\n\tfor _, field := range []string{\"passes\", \"algorithm\", \"mode\"} {\r\n\t\tif _, ok := vraw[field]; !ok {\r\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"missing required field: verification.%s\", field)\r\n\t\t}\r\n"]
[2658.074486, "o", "\t}\r\n\tswitch m.Verify.Algorithm {\r\n\tcase \"sha256\", \"blake2b\":\r\n\tdefault:\r\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid algorithm: %q (must be \\\"sha256\\\" or \\\"blake2b\\\")\", m.Verify.Algorithm)\r\n\t}\r\n\tswitch m.Verify.Mode {\r\n\tcase \"full\", \"incremental\", \"targeted\":\r\n\tdefault:\r\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid mode: %q (must be \\\"full\\\", \\\"incremental\\\", or \\\"targeted\\\")\", m.Verify.Mode)\r\n\t}\r\n\tif m.Verify.Passes < 1 {\r\n\t"]
[2658.074548, "o", "\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"passes must be >= 1, got %d\", m.Verify.Passes)\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tif m.Env.Locale == \"\" {\r\n\t\tm.Env.Locale = \"C\"\r\n\t}\r\n\tif m.Env.Timezone == \"\" {\r\n\t\tm.Env.Timezone = \"UTC\"\r\n\t}\r\n\tif m.Env.EnvVars == nil {\r\n\t\tm.Env.EnvVars = map[string]string{}\r\n\t}\r\n"]
[2658.074619, "o", "\tif m.Env.BlockedEnvVars == nil {\r\n\t\tm.Env.BlockedEnvVars = []string{}\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tif len(m.Steps) == 0 {\r\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"steps must contain at least one step\")\r\n\t}\r\n\tstepIDs := map[string]bool{}\r\n\tfor i, s := range m.Steps {\r\n\t\tif s.ID == \"\" {\r\n"]
[2658.074699, "o", "\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"missing required field: steps[%d].id\", i)\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tif !nameRe.MatchString(s.ID) {\r\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid step id: %q (must match ^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$)\", s.ID)\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tif stepIDs[s.ID] {\r\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"duplicate step id: %q\", s.ID)\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tstepIDs[s.ID] = true\r\n\t\tif s.Command == \"\" {\r\n"]
[2658.074762, "o", "\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"missing required field: steps[%d].command\", i)\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tif s.WorkingDir == \"\" {\r\n\t\t\ts.WorkingDir = \".\"\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tif s.TimeoutSecs <= 0 {\r\n\t\t\ts.TimeoutSecs = 300\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tif s.Inputs == nil {\r\n\t\t\ts.Inputs = []string{}\r\n"]
[2658.07501, "o", "\t\t}\r\n\t\tif s.Outputs == nil {\r\n\t\t\ts.Outputs = []string{}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tif s.DependsOn == nil {\r\n\t\t\ts.DependsOn = []string{}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tif s.EnvOverrides == nil {\r\n\t\t\ts.EnvOverrides = map[string]string{}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tm.Steps[i] = s\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tfor _, s := range m.Steps {\r\n\t\tfor _, dep := range s.DependsOn {\r\n\t\t\tif !stepIDs[dep] {\r\n\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"unknown dependency: step %q depends on %q\", s.ID, dep)\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tif cyc := shortestCycle(m.Steps); len(cyc) > 0 {\r\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"cycle detected: %s\", strings.Join(cyc, \" -> \"))\r\n\t}\r\n\treturn &m, nil\r\n}\r\n"]
