[2678.025859, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K1\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K Repro-Verify Specification v2\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K12\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K# 13. Verification Policy Engine\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K14\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 13.1 Policy Section in Manifest\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K40\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 13.2 Rule Schema\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K58\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 13.3 Rule Types\r\n"]
[2678.02598, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K60\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K### `allow_variance`\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K75\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K### `min_consistency_rate`\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K94\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K### `required_steps`\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K109\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K### `ignore_steps`\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K122\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 13.4 Policy Evaluation Flow\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K140\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 13.5 Report Additions\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K175\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 13.6 Exit Code with Policy\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K184\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 13.7 Policy Validation Errors\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K199\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K# 14. `diff` Subcommand\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K201\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 14.1 Usage\r\n"]
[2678.026039, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[K214\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 14.2 JSON Output Schema\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K271\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 14.3 Comparison Logic\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K302\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 14.4 Text Output Format\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K324\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 14.5 Exit Codes\r\n\u001b[32m\u001b[K332\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[01;31m\u001b[K#\u001b[m\u001b[K## 14.6 Input Validation\r\n"]
[2678.026499, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[2678.02655, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2678.324202, "i", "sed -n '1,180p' /app/docs/spec_v2.md\n"]
[2678.324529, "o", "sed -n '1,180p' /app/docs/spec_v2.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2678.327449, "o", "# Repro-Verify Specification v2\r\n\r\nThis document extends `spec_v1.md` with two major features added in v2:\r\n\r\n1. **Verification Policy Engine** — rule-based pass/fail criteria\r\n2. **`diff` Subcommand** — compare two verification reports\r\n"]
[2678.327545, "o", "\r\nAll v1 behavior remains unchanged unless explicitly overridden below.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 13. Verification Policy Engine\r\n\r\n### 13.1 Policy Section in Manifest\r\n\r\nThe manifest gains an optional `policy` section:\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"policy\": {\r\n    \"default_action\": \"strict\",\r\n    \"rules\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"id\": \"<string>\",\r\n        \"type\": \"<string>\",\r\n        \"params\": { ... },\r\n"]
[2678.327612, "o", "        \"action\": \"allow\"\r\n      }\r\n    ]\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |\r\n|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `policy` | object | no | — | If absent, strict verification applies (identical to v1 behavior). |\r\n| `policy.default_action` | string | no | `\"strict\"` | `\"strict\"`: all outputs must match. `\"lenient\"`: treat non-determinism as warnings unless a rule specifically requires a match. |\r\n| `policy.rules` | array | yes (if policy present) | — | Ordered list of policy rules. Rules are evaluated in order; the **first matching rule** for a given step/output determines the action. |\r\n\r\n"]
[2678.327672, "o", "### 13.2 Rule Schema\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"id\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"type\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"params\": { ... },\r\n  \"action\": \"<string>\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n| Field | Type | Required | Description |\r\n|-------|------|----------|-------------|\r\n"]
[2678.327727, "o", "| `id` | string | yes | Unique rule identifier. Must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`. |\r\n| `type` | string | yes | Rule type (see below). |\r\n| `params` | object | yes | Type-specific parameters. |\r\n| `action` | string | yes | `\"allow\"`, `\"warn\"`, or `\"require\"`. |\r\n\r\n### 13.3 Rule Types\r\n\r\n#### `allow_variance`\r\n\r\n"]
[2678.327782, "o", "Allows specific outputs to be non-deterministic without failing verification.\r\n\r\n**Params:**\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"output_pattern\": \"<glob pattern>\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n`output_pattern` is a glob pattern matched against output file paths (e.g., `\"*.log\"`, `\"tmp/*\"`). Uses `filepath.Match` semantics.\r\n\r\n"]
[2678.32784, "o", "**Behavior:** For outputs matching the pattern: if the output is non-deterministic (different across passes) or has a reference mismatch, and the rule's action is `\"allow\"`, the step's effective status changes from `FAIL` to `PASS` (for that output). If action is `\"warn\"`, the status stays `FAIL` but a warning is emitted. If action is `\"require\"`, the output **must** be non-deterministic (if it's actually consistent, the rule marks it as a policy violation).\r\n\r\n#### `min_consistency_rate`\r\n\r\nRequires that at least a specified fraction of passes produce identical output, but does not require 100% consistency.\r\n\r\n**Params:**\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"rate\": <float>,\r\n  \"step_pattern\": \"<glob pattern>\"\r\n"]
[2678.327899, "o", "}\r\n```\r\n\r\n- `rate`: A float between 0.0 and 1.0. For example, `0.75` means at least 75% of passes must agree.\r\n- `step_pattern`: Glob pattern matching step IDs. Use `\"*\"` for all steps.\r\n\r\n**Behavior:** For each output of matching steps, compute the **majority rate**: the fraction of passes that produced the most common fingerprint. If `majority_rate >= rate` and action is `\"allow\"`, treat the output as effectively consistent. If `majority_rate < rate` and action is `\"require\"`, it's a policy violation.\r\n\r\n**Majority rate computation:** Given N passes and fingerprints f1..fN, count occurrences of each unique fingerprint. The majority rate is `max_count / N`. For single-pass verification, majority rate is always 1.0.\r\n\r\n"]
[2678.328019, "o", "#### `required_steps`\r\n\r\nSpecifies that only certain steps are required to pass; failures in other steps don't affect the overall policy status.\r\n\r\n**Params:**\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"steps\": [\"<step_id>\", ...]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Behavior:** When evaluating policy_overall_status:\r\n- If action is `\"require\"`: all listed steps must have status PASS (after other policy rules). If any listed step is FAIL/ERROR/TIMEOUT, overall policy status is FAIL/ERROR.\r\n- If action is `\"allow\"`: unlisted steps that are FAIL/ERROR are forgiven — they don't affect policy_overall_status. Listed steps still follow normal rules.\r\n\r\n#### `ignore_steps`\r\n\r\nCompletely ignores certain steps in policy evaluation.\r\n\r\n**Params:**\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n"]
[2678.328078, "o", "  \"steps\": [\"<step_id>\", ...]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Behavior:** Steps in the list are excluded from policy_overall_status computation entirely, regardless of their actual status.\r\n\r\n### 13.4 Policy Evaluation Flow\r\n\r\n1. **Normal verification** runs first (exactly as v1), producing raw step statuses and output results.\r\n2. **Rule evaluation** in order:\r\n   - For each rule, identify which steps/outputs it matches.\r\n"]
[2678.328151, "o", "   - Apply the rule's effect based on its action:\r\n     - `\"allow\"`: If matched and the condition is satisfied, change the effective status of affected outputs/steps from FAIL→PASS.\r\n     - `\"warn\"`: If matched and the condition is satisfied, keep status but add a warning.\r\n     - `\"require\"`: If matched and the condition is NOT satisfied, mark as policy violation (FAIL).\r\n   - First matching rule wins for each output — subsequent rules don't override.\r\n3. **Recompute `policy_overall_status`:**\r\n   - After applying all rules, compute effective step statuses:\r\n     - A step is effectively PASS if all its outputs are effectively PASS (or it had no outputs / was SKIPPED).\r\n     - A step is effectively FAIL if any output is effectively FAIL.\r\n     - ERROR and TIMEOUT statuses are never changed by policy (they indicate execution failures, not verification results).\r\n   - Under `\"strict\"` default: all steps (except those matched by `ignore_steps`) must be effectively PASS for policy_overall_status=PASS.\r\n   - U"]
[2678.328216, "o", "nder `\"lenient\"` default: all steps with no matching rule that are FAIL become WARN (not FAIL), so policy_overall_status is PASS unless a `\"require\"` rule is violated.\r\n\r\n### 13.5 Report Additions\r\n\r\nThe verification report gains a `policy_evaluation` section (only present when `policy` is defined in manifest):\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"policy_evaluation\": {\r\n    \"policy_overall_status\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\",\r\n    \"default_action\": \"strict\" | \"lenient\",\r\n    \"rules_evaluated\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"rule_id\": \"<string>\",\r\n        \"rule_type\": \"<string>\",\r\n        \"matched_steps\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n        \"matched_outputs\": [\"<path>\", ...],\r\n"]
[2678.328271, "o", "        \"action\": \"allow\" | \"warn\" | \"require\",\r\n        \"effect\": \"applied\" | \"not_applicable\" | \"violation\",\r\n        \"details\": \"<string>\"\r\n      }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"effective_step_statuses\": {\r\n      \"<step_id>\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\" | \"SKIPPED\" | \"TIMEOUT\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"warnings\": [\"<string>\", ...]\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n"]
[2678.328328, "o", "```\r\n\r\n- `rules_evaluated`: One entry per rule showing what it matched and its effect.\r\n  - `\"applied\"`: The rule matched and changed something (allowed a variance, etc.)\r\n  - `\"not_applicable\"`: The rule didn't match anything or its condition wasn't relevant.\r\n  - `\"violation\"`: A `\"require\"` rule's condition was not met.\r\n- `effective_step_statuses`: Map of step ID to effective status after policy rules. Only includes steps whose effective status differs from raw status, or steps explicitly matched by a rule.\r\n- `warnings`: Human-readable warning messages from `\"warn\"` action rules.\r\n\r\n### 13.6 Exit Code with Policy\r\n\r\n"]
[2678.328381, "o", "When a policy is present, the exit code follows `policy_overall_status`:\r\n- 0: `policy_overall_status` is PASS\r\n- 1: `policy_overall_status` is FAIL\r\n- 2: `policy_overall_status` is ERROR, or manifest validation error\r\n"]
[2678.329, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[2678.329076, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2678.624985, "i", "sed -n '181,360p' /app/docs/spec_v2.md\n"]
[2678.625305, "o", "sed -n '181,360p' /app/docs/spec_v2.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2678.628633, "o", "\r\nThe raw `overall_status` in the report body is **unchanged** from v1 behavior — it still reflects the strict verification result. The policy only affects exit code and the separate `policy_evaluation` section.\r\n\r\n### 13.7 Policy Validation Errors\r\n\r\n| Error | Message |\r\n|-------|---------|\r\n| Duplicate rule ID | `error: duplicate policy rule id: \"<id>\"` |\r\n| Unknown rule type | `error: unknown policy rule type: \"<type>\"` |\r\n| Invalid action | `error: invalid policy action: \"<action>\" (must be \"allow\", \"warn\", or \"require\")` |\r\n| Invalid default_action | `error: invalid default_action: \"<value>\" (must be \"strict\" or \"lenient\")` |\r\n"]
[2678.628781, "o", "| Invalid rate | `error: invalid min_consistency_rate: rate must be between 0.0 and 1.0` |\r\n| Unknown step in required_steps | `error: unknown step in policy rule \"<rule_id>\": \"<step_id>\"` |\r\n| Unknown step in ignore_steps | `error: unknown step in policy rule \"<rule_id>\": \"<step_id>\"` |\r\n| Missing required params | `error: policy rule \"<rule_id>\" missing required param: \"<param>\"` |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 14. `diff` Subcommand\r\n\r\n### 14.1 Usage\r\n\r\n```\r\nrepro-verify diff <baseline.json> <current.json> [flags]\r\n```\r\n\r\nCompares two verification reports and outputs a structured change analysis.\r\n\r\n**Flags:**\r\n| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `--format` | string | `\"json\"` | Output format: `\"json\"` or `\"text\"`. |\r\n\r\n### 14.2 JSON Output Schema\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"baseline\": {\r\n    \"manifest_name\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"manifest_version\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"overall_status\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"timestamp\": \"<string>\"\r\n  },\r\n"]
[2678.628891, "o", "  \"current\": {\r\n    \"manifest_name\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"manifest_version\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"overall_status\": \"<string>\",\r\n    \"timestamp\": \"<string>\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"comparison_timestamp\": \"<RFC3339>\",\r\n  \"status_transition\": {\r\n    \"from\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\",\r\n    \"to\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\",\r\n    \"type\": \"regression\" | \"improvement\" | \"unchanged\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"step_changes\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"step_id\": \"<string>\",\r\n      \"change_type\": \"added\" | \"removed\" | \"modified\" | \"unchanged\",\r\n      \"baseline_status\": \"<string>\" | null,\r\n      \"current_status\": \"<string>\" | null,\r\n"]
[2678.628986, "o", "      \"status_transition\": \"regression\" | \"improvement\" | \"unchanged\" | null,\r\n      \"output_changes\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"path\": \"<string>\",\r\n          \"change_type\": \"added\" | \"removed\" | \"fingerprint_changed\" | \"consistency_changed\" | \"reference_changed\" | \"unchanged\",\r\n          \"details\": {\r\n            \"baseline_fingerprints\": [\"<fp>\", ...] | null,\r\n            \"current_fingerprints\": [\"<fp>\", ...] | null,\r\n            \"baseline_consistent\": <boolean> | null,\r\n            \"current_consistent\": <boolean> | null,\r\n            \"baseline_reference_match\": <boolean> | null,\r\n"]
[2678.629063, "o", "            \"current_reference_match\": <boolean> | null\r\n          }\r\n        }\r\n      ]\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"summary\": {\r\n    \"steps_added\": <integer>,\r\n    \"steps_removed\": <integer>,\r\n    \"steps_modified\": <integer>,\r\n    \"steps_unchanged\": <integer>,\r\n    \"regressions\": <integer>,\r\n    \"improvements\": <integer>,\r\n    \"total_output_changes\": <integer>\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n"]
[2678.629117, "o", "\r\n### 14.3 Comparison Logic\r\n\r\n**Step matching:** Steps are matched by `step_id` between baseline and current.\r\n- A step in current but not in baseline is `\"added\"`.\r\n- A step in baseline but not in current is `\"removed\"`.\r\n- A step in both is `\"modified\"` if any of its attributes changed, `\"unchanged\"` otherwise.\r\n\r\n"]
[2678.629173, "o", "**Output matching:** Within matched steps, outputs are matched by `path`.\r\n- Output change types:\r\n  - `\"added\"`: Output in current but not baseline.\r\n  - `\"removed\"`: Output in baseline but not current.\r\n  - `\"fingerprint_changed\"`: The pass-1 fingerprint differs.\r\n  - `\"consistency_changed\"`: The `cross_pass_consistent` value changed.\r\n  - `\"reference_changed\"`: The `reference_match` value changed.\r\n  - `\"unchanged\"`: No changes.\r\n  - An output can only have one `change_type`. Priority: `added` > `removed` > `fingerprint_changed` > `consistency_changed` > `reference_changed` > `unchanged`.\r\n\r\n**Status ordering for transition detection:**\r\n\r\n"]
[2678.629226, "o", "```\r\nPASS(4) > FAIL(3) > ERROR(2) > TIMEOUT(1) > SKIPPED(0)\r\n```\r\n\r\n- **Regression**: current status has lower rank than baseline status.\r\n- **Improvement**: current status has higher rank than baseline status.\r\n- **Unchanged**: same rank.\r\n\r\nThe `step_changes` array is sorted by `step_id` alphabetically.\r\n\r\n"]
[2678.629278, "o", "**The `regressions` count** in summary is the number of steps where `status_transition` is `\"regression\"`. **The `improvements` count** is the number with `\"improvement\"`.\r\n\r\n### 14.4 Text Output Format\r\n\r\n```\r\nVerification Report Diff\r\n========================\r\nBaseline: <name>@<version> (<status>) at <timestamp>\r\nCurrent:  <name>@<version> (<status>) at <timestamp>\r\nOverall:  <from> → <to> [<type>]\r\n\r\n"]
[2678.629335, "o", "Step Changes:\r\n  + <step_id> [<status>]                           # added\r\n  - <step_id> [<status>]                           # removed\r\n  ~ <step_id> [<old_status> → <new_status>]        # modified with status change\r\n  = <step_id>                                       # unchanged\r\n    Output: <path> — <change_type>                  # per output if modified\r\n\r\nSummary: <added> added, <removed> removed, <modified> modified, <unchanged> unchanged\r\n         <regressions> regressions, <improvements> improvements\r\n```\r\n"]
[2678.629387, "o", "\r\nSteps are listed in alphabetical order. Only modified steps show their output changes.\r\n\r\n### 14.5 Exit Codes\r\n\r\n| Code | Meaning |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| `0` | No regressions detected. |\r\n| `1` | At least one regression detected. |\r\n| `2` | Error (file not found, invalid JSON, not a valid verification report). |\r\n\r\n"]
[2678.629439, "o", "### 14.6 Input Validation\r\n\r\nBoth input files must be valid verification reports (containing at minimum `manifest_name`, `overall_status`, and `steps` array). If either file is missing, not valid JSON, or not a valid report, exit with code 2 and print to stderr:\r\n- `error: diff baseline not found: <path>`\r\n- `error: diff current not found: <path>`\r\n- `error: invalid report: <path>: <reason>`\r\n"]
