[2702.885161, "o", "nl -ba /app/docs/spec_v2.md | sed -n '1,220p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2702.888645, "o", "     1\t# Repro-Verify Specification v2\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tThis document extends `spec_v1.md` with two major features added in v2:\r\n     4\t\r\n"]
[2702.8887, "o", "     5\t1. **Verification Policy Engine** — rule-based pass/fail criteria\r\n     6\t2. **`diff` Subcommand** — compare two verification reports\r\n     7\t\r\n     8\tAll v1 behavior remains unchanged unless explicitly overridden below.\r\n     9\t\r\n    10\t---\r\n    11\t\r\n    12\t## 13. Verification Policy Engine\r\n    13\t\r\n"]
[2702.88887, "o", "    14\t### 13.1 Policy Section in Manifest\r\n    15\t\r\n    16\tThe manifest gains an optional `policy` section:\r\n    17\t\r\n    18\t```json\r\n    19\t{\r\n    20\t  \"policy\": {\r\n    21\t    \"default_action\": \"strict\",\r\n    22\t    \"rules\": [\r\n    23\t      {\r\n    24\t        \"id\": \"<string>\",\r\n    25\t        \"type\": \"<string>\",\r\n    26\t        \"params\": { ... },\r\n    27\t        \"action\": \"allow\"\r\n    28\t      }\r\n    29\t    ]\r\n    30\t  }\r\n    31\t}\r\n    32\t```\r\n    33\t\r\n    34\t| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |\r\n    35\t|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|\r\n    36\t| `policy` | object | no | — | If absent, strict verification applies (identical to v1 behavior). |\r\n"]
[2702.888991, "o", "    37\t| `policy.default_action` | string | no | `\"strict\"` | `\"strict\"`: all outputs must match. `\"lenient\"`: treat non-determinism as warnings unless a rule specifically requires a match. |\r\n    38\t| `policy.rules` | array | yes (if policy present) | — | Ordered list of policy rules. Rules are evaluated in order; the **first matching rule** for a given step/output determines the action. |\r\n    39\t\r\n    40\t### 13.2 Rule Schema\r\n    41\t\r\n    42\t```json\r\n    43\t{\r\n    44\t  \"id\": \"<string>\",\r\n    45\t  \"type\": \"<string>\",\r\n    46\t  \"params\": { ... },\r\n    47\t  \"action\": \"<string>\"\r\n    48\t}\r\n    49\t```\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t| Field | Type | Required | Description |\r\n    52\t|-------|------|----------|-------------|\r\n    53\t| `id` | string | yes | Unique rule identifier. Must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`. |\r\n    54\t| `type` | string | yes | Rule type (see below). |\r\n    55"]
[2702.889098, "o", "\t| `params` | object | yes | Type-specific parameters. |\r\n    56\t| `action` | string | yes | `\"allow\"`, `\"warn\"`, or `\"require\"`. |\r\n    57\t\r\n    58\t### 13.3 Rule Types\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\t#### `allow_variance`\r\n    61\t\r\n    62\tAllows specific outputs to be non-deterministic without failing verification.\r\n    63\t\r\n    64\t**Params:**\r\n    65\t```json\r\n    66\t{\r\n    67\t  \"output_pattern\": \"<glob pattern>\"\r\n    68\t}\r\n    69\t```\r\n    70\t\r\n    71\t"]
[2702.889218, "o", "`output_pattern` is a glob pattern matched against output file paths (e.g., `\"*.log\"`, `\"tmp/*\"`). Uses `filepath.Match` semantics.\r\n    72\t\r\n    73\t**Behavior:** For outputs matching the pattern: if the output is non-deterministic (different across passes) or has a reference mismatch, and the rule's action is `\"allow\"`, the step's effective status changes from `FAIL` to `PASS` (for that output). If action is `\"warn\"`, the status stays `FAIL` but a warning is emitted. If action is `\"require\"`, the output **must** be non-deterministic (if it's actually consistent, the rule marks it as a policy violation).\r\n    74\t\r\n    75\t#### `min_consistency_rate`\r\n    76\t\r\n    77\tRequires that at least a specified fraction of passes produce identical output, but does not require 100% consistency.\r\n    78\t\r\n    79\t**Params:**\r\n    80\t```json\r\n    81\t{\r\n    82\t  \"rate\": <float>,\r\n    83\t  \"step_pattern\": \"<glob pattern>\"\r\n    84\t}\r\n    85\t```\r\n"]
[2702.889287, "o", "    86\t\r\n    87\t- `rate`: A float between 0.0 and 1.0. For example, `0.75` means at least 75% of passes must agree.\r\n    88\t- `step_pattern`: Glob pattern matching step IDs. Use `\"*\"` for all steps.\r\n    89\t\r\n    90\t**Behavior:** For each output of matching steps, compute the **majority rate**: the fraction of passes that produced the most common fingerprint. If `majority_rate >= rate` and action is `\"allow\"`, treat the output as effectively consistent. If `majority_rate < rate` and action is `\"require\"`, it's a policy violation.\r\n    91\t\r\n    92\t**Majority rate computation:** Given N passes and fingerprints f1..fN, count occurrences of each unique fingerprint. The majority rate is `max_count / N`. For single-pass verification, majority rate is always 1.0.\r\n    93\t\r\n"]
[2702.889378, "o", "    94\t#### `required_steps`\r\n    95\t\r\n    96\tSpecifies that only certain steps are required to pass; failures in other steps don't affect the overall policy status.\r\n    97\t\r\n    98\t**Params:**\r\n    99\t```json\r\n   100\t{\r\n   101\t  \"steps\": [\"<step_id>\", ...]\r\n   102\t}\r\n   103\t```\r\n   104\t\r\n   105\t**Behavior:** When evaluating policy_overall_status:\r\n   106\t- If action is `\"require\"`: all listed steps must have status PASS (after other policy rules). If any listed step is FAIL/ERROR/TIMEOUT, overall policy status is FAIL/ERROR.\r\n   107\t- If action is `\"allow\"`: unlisted steps that are FAIL/ERROR are forgiven — they don't affect policy_overall_status. Listed steps still follow normal rules.\r\n   108\t\r\n   109\t#### `ignore_steps`\r\n"]
[2702.88947, "o", "   110\t\r\n   111\tCompletely ignores certain steps in policy evaluation.\r\n   112\t\r\n   113\t**Params:**\r\n   114\t```json\r\n   115\t"]
[2702.889568, "o", "{\r\n   116\t  \"steps\": [\"<step_id>\", ...]\r\n   117\t}\r\n   118\t```\r\n   119\t\r\n   120\t**Behavior:** Steps in the list are excluded from policy_overall_status computation entirely, regardless of their actual status.\r\n   121\t\r\n   122\t### 13.4 Policy Evaluation Flow\r\n   123\t\r\n   124\t1. **Normal verification** runs first (exactly as v1), producing raw step statuses and output results.\r\n   125\t2. **Rule evaluation** in order:\r\n   126\t   - For each rule, identify which steps/outputs it matches.\r\n   127\t   - Apply the rule's effect based on its action:\r\n   128\t     - `\"allow\"`: If matched and the condition is satisfied, change the effective status of affected outputs/steps from FAIL→PASS.\r\n   129\t     - `\"warn\"`: If matched and the condition is satisfied, keep status but add a warning.\r\n   130\t     - `\"require\"`: If matched and the condition is NOT satisfied, mark as policy violation (FAIL).\r\n   131\t   - First matching rule wins for each output — subsequent rules don't override.\r\n   132\t3. **Recompute `policy_overall_s"]
[2702.889666, "o", "tatus`:**\r\n   133\t   - After applying all rules, compute effective step statuses:\r\n   134\t     - A step is effectively PASS if all its outputs are effectively PASS (or it had no outputs / was SKIPPED).\r\n   135\t     - A step is effectively FAIL if any output is effectively FAIL.\r\n   136\t     - ERROR and TIMEOUT statuses are never changed by policy (they indicate execution failures, not verification results).\r\n   137\t   - Under `\"strict\"` default: all steps (except those matched by `ignore_steps`) must be effectively PASS for policy_overall_status=PASS.\r\n   138\t   - Under `\"lenient\"` default: all steps with no matching rule that are FAIL become WARN (not FAIL), so policy_overall_status is PASS unless a `\"require\"` rule is violated.\r\n   139\t\r\n   140\t### 13.5 Report Additions\r\n   141\t\r\n   142\tThe verification report gains a `policy_evaluation` section (only present when `policy` is defined in manifest):\r\n   143\t\r\n   144\t```json\r\n   145\t{\r\n   146\t  \"policy_evaluation\": {\r\n   147\t    \"policy_overall_status\": \"PASS\""]
[2702.889763, "o", " | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\",\r\n   148\t    \"default_action\": \"strict\" | \"lenient\",\r\n   149\t    \"rules_evaluated\": [\r\n   150\t      {\r\n   151\t        \"rule_id\": \"<string>\",\r\n   152\t        \"rule_type\": \"<string>\",\r\n   153\t        \"matched_steps\": [\"<step_id>\", ...],\r\n   154\t        \"matched_outputs\": [\"<path>\", ...],\r\n   155\t        \"action\": \"allow\" | \"warn\" | \"require\",\r\n   156\t        \"effect\": \"applied\" | \"not_applicable\" | \"violation\",\r\n   157\t        \"details\": \"<string>\"\r\n   158\t      }\r\n   159\t    ],\r\n   160\t    \"effective_step_statuses\": {\r\n   161\t      \"<step_id>\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\" | \"SKIPPED\" | \"TIMEOUT\"\r\n   162\t    },\r\n   163\t    \"warnings\": [\"<string>\", ...]\r\n   164\t  }\r\n   165\t}\r\n   166\t```\r\n   167\t\r\n   168\t- `rules_evaluated`: One entry per rule showing what it matched and its effect.\r\n"]
[2702.889857, "o", "   169\t  - `\"applied\"`: The rule matched and changed something (allowed a variance, etc.)\r\n   170\t  - `\"not_applicable\"`: The rule didn't match anything or its condition wasn't relevant.\r\n   171\t  - `\"violation\"`: A `\"require\"` rule's condition was not met.\r\n   172\t- `effective_step_statuses`: Map of step ID to effective status after policy rules. Only includes steps whose effective status differs from raw status, or steps explicitly matched by a rule.\r\n   173\t- `warnings`: Human-readable warning messages from `\"warn\"` action rules.\r\n   174\t\r\n   175\t### 13.6 Exit Code with Policy\r\n   176\t\r\n   177\tWhen a policy is present, the exit code follows `policy_overall_status`:\r\n   178\t- 0: `policy_overall_status` is PASS\r\n   179\t- 1: `policy_overall_status` is FAIL\r\n   180"]
[2702.890005, "o", "\t- 2: `policy_overall_status` is ERROR, or manifest validation error\r\n   181\t\r\n   182\tThe raw `overall_status` in the report body is **unchanged** from v1 behavior — it still reflects the strict verification result. The policy only affects exit code and the separate `policy_evaluation` section.\r\n   183\t\r\n   184\t### 13.7 Policy Validation Errors\r\n   185\t\r\n   186\t| Error | Message |\r\n   187\t|-------|---------|\r\n   188\t| Duplicate rule ID | `error: duplicate policy rule id: \"<id>\"` |\r\n   189\t| Unknown rule type | `error: unknown policy rule type: \"<type>\"` |\r\n   190\t| Invalid action | `error: invalid policy action: \"<action>\" (must be \"allow\", \"warn\", or \"require\")` |\r\n   191\t| Invalid default_action | `error: invalid default_action: \"<value>\" (must be \"strict\" or \"lenient\")` |\r\n   192\t| Invalid rate | `error: invalid min_consistency_rate: rate must be between 0.0 and 1.0` |\r\n   193\t| Unknown step in required_steps | `error: unknown step in policy rule \"<rule_id>\": \"<step_id>\"` |\r\n   194\t| Unknown step in igno"]
[2702.890106, "o", "re_steps | `error: unknown step in policy rule \"<rule_id>\": \"<step_id>\"` |\r\n   195\t| Missing required params | `error: policy rule \"<rule_id>\" missing required param: \"<param>\"` |\r\n   196\t\r\n   197\t---\r\n   198\t\r\n   199\t## 14. `diff` Subcommand\r\n   200\t\r\n   201\t### 14.1 Usage\r\n   202\t\r\n   203\t```\r\n   204\trepro-verify diff <baseline.json> <current.json> [flags]\r\n   205\t```\r\n   206\t\r\n   207\tCompares two verification reports and outputs a structured change analysis.\r\n   208\t\r\n   209\t**Flags:**\r\n   210\t| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n   211\t|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n   212\t| `--format` | string | `\"json\"` | Output format: `\"json\"` or `\"text\"`. |\r\n   213\t\r\n   214\t### 14.2 JSON Output Schema\r\n   215\t\r\n   216\t```json\r\n   217\t{\r\n   218\t  \"baseline\": {\r\n   219\t    \"manifest_name\": \"<string>\",\r\n"]
[2702.890163, "o", "   220\t    \"manifest_version\": \"<string>\",\r\n"]
[2702.890676, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[2702.890742, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
[2703.169403, "i", "nl -ba /app/docs/spec_v2.md | sed -n '221,360p'\n"]
[2703.169791, "o", "nl -ba /app/docs/spec_v2.md | sed -n '221,360p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2703.173677, "o", "   221\t    \"overall_status\": \"<string>\",\r\n   222\t    \"timestamp\": \"<string>\"\r\n   223\t  },\r\n   224\t  \"current\": {\r\n   225\t    \"manifest_name\": \"<string>\",\r\n   226"]
[2703.17379, "o", "\t    \"manifest_version\": \"<string>\",\r\n   227\t    \"overall_status\": \"<string>\",\r\n   228\t    \"timestamp\": \"<string>\"\r\n   229\t  },\r\n   230\t  \"comparison_timestamp\": \"<RFC3339>\",\r\n   231\t  \"status_transition\": {\r\n   232\t    \"from\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\",\r\n   233\t    \"to\": \"PASS\" | \"FAIL\" | \"ERROR\",\r\n   234\t    \"type\": \"regression\" | \"improvement\" | \"unchanged\"\r\n   235\t  },\r\n   236\t  \"step_changes\": [\r\n   237\t    {\r\n   238\t      \"step_id\": \"<string>\",\r\n   239\t      \"change_type\": \"added\" | \"removed\" | \"modified\" | \"unchanged\",\r\n   240\t      \"baseline_status\": \"<string>\" | null,\r\n   241\t      \"current_status\": \"<string>\" | null,\r\n"]
[2703.173878, "o", "   242\t      \"status_transition\": \"regression\" | \"improvement\" | \"unchanged\" | null,\r\n   243\t      \"output_changes\": [\r\n   244\t        {\r\n   245\t          \"path\": \"<string>\",\r\n   246\t          \"change_type\": \"added\" | \"removed\" | \"fingerprint_changed\" | \"consistency_changed\" | \"reference_changed\" | \"unchanged\",\r\n   247\t          \"details\": {\r\n   248\t            \"baseline_fingerprints\": [\"<fp>\", ...] | null,\r\n   249\t            \"current_fingerprints\": [\"<fp>\", ...] | null,\r\n   250\t            \"baseline_consistent\": <boolean> | null,\r\n   251\t            \"current_consistent\": <boolean> | null,\r\n   252\t            \"baseline_reference_match\": <boolean> | null,\r\n   253\t            \"current_reference_match\": <boolean> | null\r\n"]
[2703.173991, "o", "   254\t          }\r\n   255\t        }\r\n   256\t      ]\r\n   257\t    }\r\n   258\t  ],\r\n   259\t  \"summary\": {\r\n   260\t    \"steps_added\": <integer>,\r\n   261\t    \"steps_removed\": <integer>,\r\n   262\t    \"steps_modified\": <integer>,\r\n   263\t    \"steps_unchanged\": <integer>,\r\n   264\t    \"regressions\": <integer>,\r\n   265\t    \"improvements\": <integer>,\r\n   266\t    \"total_output_changes\": <integer>\r\n   267\t  }\r\n   268\t}\r\n   269\t```\r\n"]
[2703.174071, "o", "   270\t\r\n   271\t### 14.3 Comparison Logic\r\n   272\t\r\n   273\t**Step matching:** Steps are matched by `step_id` between baseline and current.\r\n   274\t- A step in current but not in baseline is `\"added\"`.\r\n   275\t- A step in baseline but not in current is `\"removed\"`.\r\n   276\t- A step in both is `\"modified\"` if any of its attributes changed, `\"unchanged\"` otherwise.\r\n   277\t\r\n   278\t**Output matching:** Within matched steps, outputs are matched by `path`.\r\n   279\t- Output change types:\r\n   280\t  - `\"added\"`: Output in current but not baseline.\r\n   281\t  - `\"removed\"`: Output in baseline but not current.\r\n"]
[2703.174143, "o", "   282\t  - `\"fingerprint_changed\"`: The pass-1 fingerprint differs.\r\n   283\t  - `\"consistency_changed\"`: The `cross_pass_consistent` value changed.\r\n   284\t  - `\"reference_changed\"`: The `reference_match` value changed.\r\n   285\t  - `\"unchanged\"`: No changes.\r\n   286\t  - An output can only have one `change_type`. Priority: `added` > `removed` > `fingerprint_changed` > `consistency_changed` > `reference_changed` > `unchanged`.\r\n   287\t\r\n   288\t**Status ordering for transition detection:**\r\n   289\t\r\n   290\t```\r\n   291\tPASS(4) > FAIL(3) > ERROR(2) > TIMEOUT(1) > SKIPPED(0)\r\n   292\t"]
[2703.174221, "o", "```\r\n   293\t\r\n   294\t- **Regression**: current status has lower rank than baseline status.\r\n   295\t- **Improvement**: current status has higher rank than baseline status.\r\n   296\t- **Unchanged**: same rank.\r\n   297\t\r\n   298\tThe `step_changes` array is sorted by `step_id` alphabetically.\r\n   299\t\r\n   300\t**The `regressions` count** in summary is the number of steps where `status_transition` is `\"regression\"`. **The `improvements` count** is the number with `\"improvement\"`.\r\n   301\t\r\n   302\t### 14.4 Text Output Format\r\n"]
[2703.174348, "o", "   303\t\r\n   304\t```\r\n   305\tVerification Report Diff\r\n   306\t========================\r\n   307\tBaseline: <name>@<version> (<status>) at <timestamp>\r\n   308\tCurrent:  <name>@<version> (<status>) at <timestamp>\r\n   309\tOverall:  <from> → <to> [<type>]\r\n   310\t\r\n   311\tStep Changes:\r\n   312\t  + <step_id> [<status>]                           # added\r\n   313\t  - <step_id> [<status>]                           # removed\r\n   314\t  ~ <step_id> [<old_status> → <new_status>]        # modified with status change\r\n   315\t  = <step_id>                                       # unchanged\r\n   316\t    Output: <path> — <change_type>                  # per output if modified\r\n   317\t\r\n   318\tSummary: <added> added, <removed> removed, <modified> modified, <unchanged> unchanged\r\n   319\t"]
[2703.174449, "o", "         <regressions> regressions, <improvements> improvements\r\n   320\t```\r\n   321\t\r\n   322\tSteps are listed in alphabetical order. Only modified steps show their output changes.\r\n   323\t\r\n   324\t### 14.5 Exit Codes\r\n   325\t\r\n   326\t| Code | Meaning |\r\n   327\t|------|---------|\r\n   328\t| `0` | No regressions detected. |\r\n   329\t| `1` | At least one regression detected. |\r\n   330\t| `2` | Error (file not found, invalid JSON, not a valid verification report). |\r\n   331\t\r\n   332\t### 14.6 Input Validation\r\n   333\t\r\n   334\tBoth input files must be valid verification reports (containing at minimum `manifest_name`, `overall_status`, and `steps` array). If either file is missing, not valid JSON, or not a valid report, exit with code 2 and print to stderr:\r\n"]
[2703.174517, "o", "   335\t- `error: diff baseline not found: <path>`\r\n   336\t- `error: diff current not found: <path>`\r\n   337\t- `error: invalid report: <path>: <reason>`\r\n"]
