[2755.792569, "o", "nl -ba /app/docs/spec_v2.md | sed -n '12,39p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[2755.795972, "o", "    12\t## 13. Verification Policy Engine\r\n    13\t\r\n    14\t### 13.1 Policy Section in Manifest\r\n    15\t\r\n    16\tThe manifest gains an optional `policy` section:\r\n    17\t\r\n    18\t"]
[2755.796098, "o", "```json\r\n    19\t{\r\n    20\t  \"policy\": {\r\n    21\t    \"default_action\": \"strict\",\r\n    22\t    \"rules\": [\r\n    23\t      {\r\n    24\t        \"id\": \"<string>\",\r\n    25\t        \"type\": \"<string>\",\r\n    26\t        \"params\": { ... },\r\n    27\t        \"action\": \"allow\"\r\n    28\t      }\r\n    29\t    ]\r\n    30\t  }\r\n    31\t}\r\n    32\t```\r\n    33\t\r\n    34\t| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |\r\n    35\t|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|\r\n    36\t| `policy` | object | no | — | If absent, strict verification applies (identical to v1 behavior). |\r\n    37\t| `policy.default_action` | string | no | `\"strict\"` | `\"strict\"`: all outputs must match. `\"lenient\"`: treat non-determinism as warnings unless a rule specifically requires a match. |\r\n    38\t| `policy.rules` | array | yes (if policy present) | — | Ordered list of policy rules. Rules are evaluated in order; the **first matching rule** for a given step/output determines the action. |\r\n    39\t\r\n"]
[2755.796742, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
