[2756.069371, "o", "    40\t### 13.2 Rule Schema\r\n    41\t\r\n    42\t```json\r\n    43\t{\r\n    44\t  \"id\": \"<string>\",\r\n    45\t  \"type\": \"<string>\",\r\n    46\t  \"params\": { ... },\r\n    47"]
[2756.069563, "o", "\t  \"action\": \"<string>\"\r\n    48\t}\r\n    49\t```\r\n    50\t\r\n    51\t| Field | Type | Required | Description |\r\n    52\t|-------|------|----------|-------------|\r\n    53\t| `id` | string | yes | Unique rule identifier. Must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$`. |\r\n"]
[2756.069658, "o", "    54\t| `type` | string | yes | Rule type (see below). |\r\n    55\t| `params` | object | yes | Type-specific parameters. |\r\n    56\t| `action` | string | yes | `\"allow\"`, `\"warn\"`, or `\"require\"`. |\r\n    57\t\r\n    58\t### 13.3 Rule Types\r\n    59\t\r\n    60\t#### `allow_variance`\r\n    61\t\r\n    62\tAllows specific outputs to be non-deterministic without failing verification.\r\n    63\t\r\n    64\t**Params:**\r\n    65\t```json\r\n    66\t{\r\n    67\t  \"output_pattern\": \"<glob pattern>\"\r\n    68\t}\r\n    69\t```\r\n    70\t\r\n    71\t`output_pattern` is a glob pattern matched against output file paths (e.g., `\"*.log\"`, `\"tmp/*\"`). Uses `filepath.Match` semantics.\r\n    72\t\r\n    73\t**Behavior:** For outputs matching the pattern: if the output is non-deterministic (different across passes) or has a reference mismatch, and the rule's action is `\"allow\"`, the step's effective status changes from `FAIL` to `PASS` (for that output). If action is `\"warn\"`, the status stays `FAIL` but a warning is emitted. If action is `\"require\"`, the output **must*"]
[2756.069729, "o", "* be non-deterministic (if it's actually consistent, the rule marks it as a policy violation).\r\n    74\t\r\n    75\t#### `min_consistency_rate`\r\n    76\t\r\n"]
[2756.070167, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
