[3777.283033, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3777.286148, "o", "# Repro-Verify Specification v3\r\n\r\nThis document extends `spec_v2.md` with corrections and one new feature added in v3.\r\n\r\nAll v1 and v2 behavior remains unchanged unless explicitly overridden below.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 15. Corrections to v2\r\n\r\n### 15.1 Policy Engine: Raw Status Preservation\r\n\r\n**Correction**: Section 13.6 of spec_v2 stated that the raw `overall_status` is unchanged, but the requirement was not enforced strictly enough. This is now a hard requirement:\r\n\r\n- The `overall_status` field in the verification report MUST always reflect the strict v1 verification result, regardless of any policy rules.\r\n- A non-deterministic pipeline that would produce `overall_status: \"FAIL\"` under v1 rules MUST still show `overall_status: \"FAIL\"` even if a policy rule allows the variance.\r\n"]
[3777.286327, "o", "- The policy engine affects ONLY:\r\n  1. The `policy_evaluation` section of the report\r\n  2. The process exit code\r\n- Any implementation that modifies `overall_status` based on policy rules is incorrect.\r\n\r\n### 15.2 Diff Subcommand: Exit Code on Regression\r\n\r\n**Correction**: The diff subcommand exit code behavior (spec_v2 Section 14.5) must be strictly enforced:\r\n\r\n- Exit code `1` MUST be returned when any step has a `status_transition` of type `\"regression\"` (i.e., when `summary.regressions >= 1`).\r\n- Exit code `0` is returned ONLY when there are zero regressions, even if there are improvements or other changes.\r\n- Exit code `2` is for errors (file not found, invalid JSON).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 16. Summary Subcommand\r\n\r\n### 16.1 Usage\r\n\r\n```\r\nrepro-verify summary <report1.json> [report2.json ...]\r\n```\r\n\r\nReads one or more verification report JSON files and produces a concise summary.\r\n\r\n**Flags:**\r\n| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n| `--format` | string | `\"json\"` | Out"]
[3777.286417, "o", "put format: `\"json\"` or `\"text\"`. |\r\n\r\n### 16.2 JSON Output Schema\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"summary_timestamp\": \"<RFC3339>\",\r\n  \"reports\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"file\": \"<path>\",\r\n      \"manifest_name\": \"<string>\",\r\n      \"manifest_version\": \"<string>\",\r\n      \"overall_status\": \"<string>\",\r\n      \"step_count\": <integer>,\r\n      \"pass_count\": <integer>,\r\n      \"fail_count\": <integer>,\r\n      \"pass_rate\": <float>\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"aggregate\": {"]
[3777.286497, "o", "\r\n    \"total_reports\": <integer>,\r\n    \"total_steps\": <integer>,\r\n    \"total_pass\": <integer>,\r\n    \"total_fail\": <integer>,\r\n    \"overall_pass_rate\": <float>,\r\n    \"all_passing\": <boolean>\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Field details:**\r\n- `reports`: One entry per input file, in the order provided on the command line.\r\n- `file`: The file path as given on the command line.\r\n- `step_count`: Total number of steps in the report.\r\n- `pass_count`: Number of steps with status `\"PASS\"`.\r\n- `fail_count`: Number of steps with status other than `\"PASS\"` (includes `\"FAIL\"`, `\"ERROR\"`, `\"TIMEOUT\"`, `\"SKIPPED\"`).\r\n"]
[3777.286582, "o", "- `pass_rate`: `pass_count / step_count`, as a float between 0.0 and 1.0. If `step_count` is 0, `pass_rate` is 1.0.\r\n- `aggregate.total_steps`: Sum of all `step_count` values.\r\n- `aggregate.total_pass`: Sum of all `pass_count` values.\r\n- `aggregate.total_fail`: Sum of all `fail_count` values.\r\n- `aggregate.overall_pass_rate`: `total_pass / total_steps`. If `total_steps` is 0, 1.0.\r\n- `aggregate.all_passing`: `true` if every report has `overall_status == \"PASS\"`, `false` otherwise.\r\n\r\n### 16.3 Text Output Format\r\n\r\n```\r\n<manifest_name>@<version>  <overall_status>  <pass_count>/<step_count> steps  (<pass_rate_pct>%)\r\n...\r\n---\r\n<total_reports> reports, <total_steps> total steps, <overall_pass_rate_pct>% pass rate\r\n```\r\n\r\nEach report is on one line. The pass rate percentage is formatted to one decimal place (e.g., `66.7%`, `100.0%`). Reports are listed in input order.\r\n\r\n### 16.4 Exit Codes\r\n\r\n| Code | Meaning |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| `0` | All reports have `overall_status == \"PASS\"`. |\r\n| `1` | At least one repo"]
[3777.286654, "o", "rt has `overall_status != \"PASS\"`. |\r\n| `2` | Error (file not found, invalid JSON, not a valid report, no arguments). |\r\n\r\n### 16.5 Input Validation\r\n\r\n- At least one report file must be provided. If no arguments are given, exit with code 2 and print: `error: summary requires at least one report file`.\r\n- Each file must exist, be valid JSON, and contain at minimum `manifest_name`, `overall_status`, and `steps` array. If any file fails validation, exit with code 2 and print to stderr:\r\n  - `error: summary file not found: <path>`\r\n  - `error: invalid summary input: <path>: <reason>`\r\n"]
[3777.287166, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[3777.287236, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
