[5404.63161, "i", "nl -ba docs/spec_v4.md\n"]
[5404.631896, "o", "nl -ba docs/spec_v4.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[5404.634509, "o", "     1\t# Repro-Verify Specification v4\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tThis document extends `spec_v3.md` with one new feature added in v4.\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\tAll v1, v2, and v3 behavior remains unchanged unless explicitly overridden below.\r\n     6\t\r\n     7\t---\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t## 17. Trend Analysis Subcommand\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\t### 17.1 Usage\r\n"]
[5404.634701, "o", "    12\t\r\n    13\t```\r\n    14\trepro-verify trend <report1.json> <report2.json> [report3.json ...]\r\n    15\t```\r\n    16\t\r\n    17\tReads two or more verification report JSON files in chronological order (first argument = oldest, last argument = newest) and produces a trend analysis showing how per-step verification results change over time.\r\n    18\t\r\n    19\t**Flags:**\r\n    20\t| Flag | Type | Default | Description |\r\n"]
[5404.634797, "o", "    21\t|------|------|---------|-------------|\r\n    22\t| `--format` | string | `\"json\"` | Output format: `\"json\"` or `\"text\"`. |\r\n    23\t\r\n    24\t### 17.2 JSON Output Schema\r\n    25\t\r\n    26\t```json\r\n    27\t{\r\n    28\t  \"trend_timestamp\": \"<RFC3339>\",\r\n    29\t  \"report_count\": <integer>,\r\n    30\t  \"step_trends\": [\r\n    31\t    {\r\n    32\t      \"step_id\": \"<string>\",\r\n    33\t      \"statuses\": [\"PASS\", null, \"FAIL\", ...],\r\n    34\t      \"first_seen_index\": <integer>,\r\n    35\t      \"last_seen_index\": <integer>,\r\n    36\t      \"status_changes\": <integer>,\r\n    37\t      \"stability\": <float>,\r\n    38\t      \"classification\": \"<stable|flaky|degrading|improving>\"\r\n    39\t    }\r\n    40\t  ],\r\n    41\t  \"aggregate\": {\r\n    42\t    \"total_steps_tracked\": <integer>,\r\n    43\t    \"stable_count\": <integer>,\r\n    44\t    \"flaky_count\": <integer>,\r\n    45\t    \"degrading_count\": <integer>,\r\n    46\t    \"improving_count\": <integer>,\r\n"]
[5404.634869, "o", "    47\t    \"overall_stability\": <float>\r\n    48\t  }\r\n    49\t}\r\n    50\t```\r\n    51\t\r\n    52\t**Field details:**\r\n    53\t\r\n    54\t- `report_count`: Number of input report files.\r\n    55\t- `step_trends`: One entry per unique step ID found across all reports. Sorted alphabetically by `step_id`.\r\n    56\t- `statuses`: Array of length `report_count`. For each report (in input order), the status string of this step in that report, or `null` (JSON null) if the step is not present in that report.\r\n    57\t- `first_seen_index`: 0-based index of the first report where this step appears (status is not null).\r\n    58\t- `last_seen_index`: 0-based index of the last report where this step appears (status is not null).\r\n"]
[5404.634956, "o", "    59\t- `status_changes`: Number of times the status changed between consecutive non-null entries. Only transitions between non-null statuses count. If a step appears in reports 0, 2, 4 (missing in 1, 3), compare status at index 0 with status at index 2, then index 2 with index 4.\r\n    60\t- `stability`: Calculated as `1.0 - (status_changes / (appearances - 1))`, where `appearances` is the count of non-null entries in `statuses`. If `appearances <= 1`, stability is `1.0`.\r\n    61\t- `classification`: Determined by the following rules applied in order:\r\n    62\t"]
[5404.635041, "o", "  1. If `status_changes == 0`: `\"stable\"`\r\n    63\t  2. If `status_changes >= 2`: `\"flaky\"`\r\n    64\t  3. If `status_changes == 1` and the last non-null status has a **lower** rank than the first non-null status: `\"degrading\"`\r\n    65\t  4. If `status_changes == 1` and the last non-null status has a **higher** rank than the first non-null status: `\"improving\"`\r\n    66\t\r\n    67\t  Status ranks (higher is better): `PASS` = 4, `FAIL` = 3, `ERROR` = 2, `TIMEOUT` = 1, `SKIPPED` = 0.\r\n    68\t\r\n    69\t**Aggregate fields:**\r\n    70\t"]
[5404.63511, "o", "- `total_steps_tracked`: Total number of unique step IDs across all reports.\r\n    71\t- `stable_count`: Number of steps with classification `\"stable\"`.\r\n    72\t- `flaky_count`: Number of steps with classification `\"flaky\"`.\r\n    73\t- `degrading_count`: Number of steps with classification `\"degrading\"`.\r\n    74\t- `improving_count`: Number of steps with classification `\"improving\"`.\r\n    75\t- `overall_stability`: Average of all steps' `stability` values. If `total_steps_tracked == 0`, `1.0`.\r\n    76\t\r\n    77\t### 17.3 Text Output Format\r\n    78\t\r\n    79\t```\r\n    80\tTrend Analysis (<N> reports)\r\n    81\t==========================\r\n    82\t"]
[5404.635183, "o", "<step_id>  <classification>  [<s1>, <s2>, ...]  stability=<value>\r\n    83\t...\r\n    84\t---\r\n    85\t<total> steps: <stable> stable, <flaky> flaky, <degrading> degrading, <improving> improving\r\n    86\tOverall stability: <pct>%\r\n    87\t```\r\n    88\t\r\n    89\t- Each step on one line. Status values are comma-separated. Null entries display as `-`.\r\n    90\t- Stability value is formatted to two decimal places (e.g., `0.50`, `1.00`).\r\n    91\t- Overall stability percentage is formatted to one decimal place (e.g., `75.0%`, `100.0%`).\r\n    92\t- Steps are listed in alphabetical order by `step_id`.\r\n    93\t\r\n    94\t### 17.4 Exit Codes\r\n"]
[5404.63531, "o", "    95\t\r\n    96\t| Code | Meaning |\r\n    97\t|------|---------|\r\n    98\t| `0` | No degrading or flaky steps detected. |\r\n    99\t| `1` | At least one step is classified as `\"degrading\"` or `\"flaky\"`. |\r\n   100\t| `2` | Error (file not found, invalid JSON, fewer than 2 report files). |\r\n   101\t\r\n"]
[5404.635378, "o", "   102\t### 17.5 Input Validation\r\n   103\t\r\n   104\t- At least two report files must be provided. If fewer than two arguments are given, exit with code 2 and print: `error: trend requires at least two report files`.\r\n   105\t- Each file must exist, be valid JSON, and contain at minimum `manifest_name`, `overall_status`, and `steps` array. If any file fails validation, exit with code 2 and print to stderr:\r\n   106\t  - `error: trend file not found: <path>`\r\n   107\t  - `error: invalid trend input: <path>: <reason>`\r\n"]
[5404.635711, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[5404.635777, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
