[5888.436595, "o", "drwxr-xr-x 2 root root  4096 Jul 21 12:55 \u001b[0m\u001b[01;34m.\u001b[0m\r\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root  4096 Sep  7 10:31 \u001b[01;34m..\u001b[0m\r\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 root root 22341 Apr  8 17:05 spec_v1.md\r\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 root root 13217 Apr  9 11:45 spec_v2.md\r\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 root root  4341 Apr  9 12:47 spec_v3.md\r\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 root root  4681 Apr  9 13:33 spec_v4.md\r\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 root root  3337 Apr  9 14:31 spec_v5.md\r\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 root root  1494 Apr  9 14:45 spec_v6.md\r\n"]
[5888.436677, "o", "-rw-rw-r-- 1 root root  1499 Apr  9 14:45 spec_v7.md\r\n"]
[5888.43985, "o", "# Repro-Verify Specification v5\r\n\r\nThis document extends `spec_v4.md` with one correction and one new feature.\r\n\r\nAll v1, v2, v3, and v4 behavior remains unchanged unless explicitly overridden below.\r\n"]
[5888.439925, "o", "\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 18. Corrections to v4 — Trend Status Ranks\r\n\r\n### 18.1 Revised Status Ranks\r\n\r\nThe status ranks used by the `trend` subcommand (Section 17.2) for `classification` are revised:\r\n\r\n**Previous (v4) ranks:**\r\n| Status | Rank |\r\n|--------|------|\r\n| `PASS` | 4 |\r\n| `FAIL` | 3 |\r\n| `ERROR` | 2 |\r\n| `TIMEOUT` | 1 |\r\n| `SKIPPED` | 0 |\r\n\r\n"]
[5888.440036, "o", "**Corrected (v5) ranks:**\r\n| Status | Rank |\r\n|--------|------|\r\n| `PASS` | 4 |\r\n| `TIMEOUT` | 3 |\r\n| `ERROR` | 2 |\r\n| `FAIL` | 1 |\r\n| `SKIPPED` | 0 |\r\n\r\n**Rationale:** A `TIMEOUT` indicates the step ran but exceeded its time limit — it was closer to completing. A `FAIL` indicates the step produced incorrect results — a fundamental correctness issue. `ERROR` represents an unrecoverable runtime error, between the two.\r\n\r\nThis correction affects the `classification` field for any trend entries involving transitions between `FAIL`, `ERROR`, and `TIMEOUT`. The `stability` calculation is unaffected because it only counts status changes, not their direction.\r\n\r\n**Note:** The `diff` subcommand (Section 14) uses its own status rank map for determining regressions/improvements. The diff ranks are **unchanged** and remain as defined in v2: `PASS` > `FAIL` > `ERROR` > `TIMEOUT` > `SKIPPED`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n"]
[5888.440104, "o", "\r\n## 19. Slice Subcommand\r\n\r\n### 19.1 Usage\r\n\r\n```\r\n"]
[5888.440167, "o", "repro-verify slice <report.json> --status <STATUS> [--status <STATUS> ...]\r\n```\r\n\r\nReads a verification report JSON file and extracts only the steps matching the specified status filter(s). The `--status` flag can be provided multiple times for OR matching.\r\n\r\n### 19.2 JSON Output Schema\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"source_file\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"manifest_name\": \"<string>\",\r\n  \"filter_statuses\": [\"<STATUS1>\", \"<STATUS2>\"],\r\n  \"total_steps\": <integer>,\r\n  \"matched_count\": <integer>,\r\n  \"steps\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"<string>\",\r\n      \"status\": \"<string>\"\r\n    }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n"]
[5888.440234, "o", "**Field details:**\r\n\r\n- `source_file`: The path of the input report file (as provided on the command line).\r\n- `manifest_name`: The `manifest_name` from the input report.\r\n- `filter_statuses`: Array of status strings that were used as filters, in the order provided.\r\n- `total_steps`: Total number of steps in the original report.\r\n- `matched_count`: Number of steps matching any of the filter statuses.\r\n- `steps`: Array of step objects from the report that match the filter. Each step object contains at minimum the `id` and `status` fields. Steps are listed in the same order as they appear in the original report.\r\n\r\n### 19.3 Exit Codes\r\n\r\n| Code | Meaning |\r\n|------|---------|\r\n| `0` | At least one step matched the filter. |\r\n"]
[5888.440296, "o", "| `1` | No steps matched the filter (matched_count is 0). |\r\n| `2` | Error (file not found, invalid JSON, no `--status` flag provided). |\r\n\r\n### 19.4 Input Validation\r\n\r\n- At least one `--status` flag must be provided. If no `--status` flag is given, exit with code 2 and print to stderr: `error: slice requires at least one --status flag`.\r\n- The input file must exist and be valid JSON containing at minimum `manifest_name`, `overall_status`, and `steps` array. If validation fails, exit with code 2 and print to stderr:\r\n  - `error: slice file not found: <path>`\r\n  - `error: invalid slice input: <path>: <reason>`\r\n"]
[5888.440818, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[5888.440877, "o", "root@n30009:/app# "]
